{"jobs":[{"id":"87e4fac9-9193-40d7-9b28-dbc73e55615c","title":"Software Engineer, Product Platform","department":"Engineering","team":"Platform Services","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York, NY","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Arlington, VA","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Virginia","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Arlington"}}}],"publishedAt":"2023-06-16T21:04:51.192+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"450 Park Avenue South","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/87e4fac9-9193-40d7-9b28-dbc73e55615c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/87e4fac9-9193-40d7-9b28-dbc73e55615c/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Cape</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected <em>and</em> have privacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>The Role</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Product Platform team owns the foundational services that power Cape: Identity &amp; Access, Subscriber Lifecycle, Provisioning, Billing, Reporting, Spam Protection, and Voicemail. You will work closely with Product, Mobile, and SRE teams to enable new features, and you will own features that span multiple foundational components end to end.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re hiring engineers who are passionate about solving real-world problems, personal privacy, and empowering peers to be autonomous. Our team needs experienced engineers who have strong distributed systems backgrounds to help us re-architect these systems as we scale into our next phase. This includes re-organizing services for maintainability and extensibility as we grow in features and people, and adopting the right service infrastructure (workflow orchestration, service tooling, CI/CD) and data infrastructure (Postgres, Redis, streaming materialized views, data lake). Your day-to-day will constantly change and be filled with ambiguity, but everything you work on has a high impact.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Cape is a flat organization and we don't have formal levels. For calibration: this is a <strong>Senior/Staff</strong> scope role - you'll own architecture across systems and make decisions that stick.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What You'll Work On</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Enable Scale</strong>:  Build reliable, extensible systems that let us grow in features, users, and engineers including re-architecting existing services and migrating live flows onto new systems safely.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the Lifecycle</strong>: Take full ownership of features that span multiple foundational components from problem discovery through design, deployment, and operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raise the Bar</strong>: Make safe change the default - end-to-end testing, continuous deployment, zero-downtime migrations, and hold a high standard through design and code review.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate</strong>: Work closely with Product, Mobile, SRE, and Design to shape features and the infrastructure they run on, bringing stakeholders along through clear written proposals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mentor</strong>: Grow the engineers around you through pairing, review, and written designs, transferring ownership of what you build.<br /></p></li></ul><h1>What We Value</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Autonomy:</strong> A proven ability to learn continuously, work independently, and make decisions with minimal supervision.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partnership: </strong>Experience brainstorming and iterating alongside product managers and designers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Pragmatism: </strong>The ability to move quickly while building for the long term. You take a thoughtful, practical approach to solving complex problems, considering tradeoffs and avoiding over-engineering.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Adaptability: </strong>Comfort working in a constantly evolving environment with dynamic objectives and direct user iteration.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Communication: </strong>The ability to work collaboratively with both technical and non-technical teammates, understanding how technical decisions impact the end user.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mission-Driven:</strong> A deep-seated belief in the importance of digital privacy and security. You understand that the code we ship has real-world consequences and are driven to build systems that protect and empower users.<br /></p></li></ul><h1>Experience</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of experience building and operating scalable backend systems in one or more modern languages (we're primarily a Go shop).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong foundation in Computer Science - algorithms, data structures, and distributed systems demonstrated through the systems you've built.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on distributed systems experience: you've designed and operated services that communicate through queues and async workflows, and you know idempotency, retries, and schema migrations from production experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading a significant re-architecture or migration on a live system, end to end.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal communication skills - you work through designs and decisions in writing and bring others along.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Compensation</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive compensation that is <strong>geo-adjusted</strong> based on <strong>your location</strong>, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in NYC is $200K - $290K depending on level, experience, and interview performance. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our benefits include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stipends for </p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Family-forming needs </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gender-affirming care </p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Culture &amp; Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How to apply</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Click the link below to apply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT CAPE\n\nCape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.\n\nInstead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected and have privacy.\n\nWe didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.\n\nToday, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM\n\nAt Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nThe Product Platform team owns the foundational services that power Cape: Identity & Access, Subscriber Lifecycle, Provisioning, Billing, Reporting, Spam Protection, and Voicemail. You will work closely with Product, Mobile, and SRE teams to enable new features, and you will own features that span multiple foundational components end to end.\n\n\n\nWe’re hiring engineers who are passionate about solving real-world problems, personal privacy, and empowering peers to be autonomous. Our team needs experienced engineers who have strong distributed systems backgrounds to help us re-architect these systems as we scale into our next phase. This includes re-organizing services for maintainability and extensibility as we grow in features and people, and adopting the right service infrastructure (workflow orchestration, service tooling, CI/CD) and data infrastructure (Postgres, Redis, streaming materialized views, data lake). Your day-to-day will constantly change and be filled with ambiguity, but everything you work on has a high impact.\n\n\n\nCape is a flat organization and we don't have formal levels. For calibration: this is a Senior/Staff scope role - you'll own architecture across systems and make decisions that stick.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL WORK ON\n\n - Enable Scale:  Build reliable, extensible systems that let us grow in features, users, and engineers including re-architecting existing services and migrating live flows onto new systems safely.\n\n - Own the Lifecycle: Take full ownership of features that span multiple foundational components from problem discovery through design, deployment, and operations.\n\n - Raise the Bar: Make safe change the default - end-to-end testing, continuous deployment, zero-downtime migrations, and hold a high standard through design and code review.\n\n - Collaborate: Work closely with Product, Mobile, SRE, and Design to shape features and the infrastructure they run on, bringing stakeholders along through clear written proposals.\n\n - Mentor: Grow the engineers around you through pairing, review, and written designs, transferring ownership of what you build.\n   \n\n\nWHAT WE VALUE\n\n - Autonomy: A proven ability to learn continuously, work independently, and make decisions with minimal supervision.\n\n - Partnership: Experience brainstorming and iterating alongside product managers and designers.\n\n - Pragmatism: The ability to move quickly while building for the long term. You take a thoughtful, practical approach to solving complex problems, considering tradeoffs and avoiding over-engineering.\n\n - Adaptability: Comfort working in a constantly evolving environment with dynamic objectives and direct user iteration.\n\n - Communication: The ability to work collaboratively with both technical and non-technical teammates, understanding how technical decisions impact the end user.\n\n - Mission-Driven: A deep-seated belief in the importance of digital privacy and security. You understand that the code we ship has real-world consequences and are driven to build systems that protect and empower users.\n   \n\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n - 7+ years of experience building and operating scalable backend systems in one or more modern languages (we're primarily a Go shop).\n\n - A strong foundation in Computer Science - algorithms, data structures, and distributed systems demonstrated through the systems you've built.\n\n - Hands-on distributed systems experience: you've designed and operated services that communicate through queues and async workflows, and you know idempotency, retries, and schema migrations from production experience.\n\n - Experience leading a significant re-architecture or migration on a live system, end to end.\n\n - Strong written and verbal communication skills - you work through designs and decisions in writing and bring others along.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nWe offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in NYC is $200K - $290K depending on level, experience, and interview performance. \n\nOur benefits include:\n\n - 401(k) match\n\n - 100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents\n\n - 12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)\n\n - Stipends for \n   \n   - Family-forming needs \n   \n   - Gender-affirming care \n\n - Unlimited PTO\n\n\n\n\nOUR CULTURE & VALUES\n\n - We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.\n\n - We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.\n\n - We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.\n\n - We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nClick the link below to apply.\n\nWe reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.\n\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"72b03d27-d02b-4aca-915d-b9409feff11b","title":"Software Engineer, iOS","department":"Engineering","team":"Mobile","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York, NY","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-09T19:28:16.885+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"450 Park Avenue South","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/72b03d27-d02b-4aca-915d-b9409feff11b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/72b03d27-d02b-4aca-915d-b9409feff11b/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Cape</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected <em>and</em> have privacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>The Role</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape’s platform gives customers end-to-end control of their digital identity, optimizing for resiliency, privacy, and security at every turn. We’re transforming how customers sign up, use, and think about their mobile phones and the privacy implications associated with it. Customers are protected at every level of the communications stack – from the mobile device, through infrastructure, and to the core of the network itself.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an iOS Engineer at Cape, your mission is to build the definitive application for private mobile communication. We don’t just white label an application and do the bare minimum for onboarding and collecting payment. The mobile application is the interface where users build trust with Cape and protect their digital lives. You will own the entire feature lifecycle—from architectural design to App Store launch - using Swift and SwiftUI to solve some of the hardest technical challenges in security and cryptography in order to secure personal information (PII), account data, and even voice &amp; SMS traffic. In our tight-knit engineering team, you won't just build features; you will ship the product that makes our promise of privacy a reality.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your day-to-day will change, but everything you work on has a high impact. One day you could be pushing to deliver a new capability to prevent targeting of soldiers on the battlefield, the next you could be architecting a new system to prevent financial fraud via SIM swaps for everyday citizens.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Work On</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Take ownership of the mobile product lifecycle, from conceptualization, through design &amp; development, all the way to launch.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain high coding standards through the development of guidelines, active participation in code reviews, and fostering a culture of continuous improvement and knowledge sharing among your team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Champion the security, performance, and stability of our applications. You will implement and oversee robust testing, monitoring, and release processes to guarantee a seamless and trustworthy user experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actively improve user workflows by collaborating with cross-functional teams, ensuring seamless experiences across product boundaries and a cohesive user experience.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What We Value</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to learn continuously, work independently, and make decisions with minimal supervision.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience brainstorming and iterating with product designers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to take a thoughtful, practical approach to problem-solving that considers tradeoffs and avoids over-engineering.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Skill and comfort working in a constantly evolving environment with dynamic objectives and iteration with users.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work collaboratively in teams of technical and non-technical individuals and understand how technical decisions impact the people who will use what you're building.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of cryptographic systems and how to design privacy conscious solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to learn new technology and concepts, even without in-depth experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Experience</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of iOS software development experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engineering background in Computer Science, Mathematics, Software Engineering, Physics or similar field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in Swift and a strong foundational understanding of the iOS ecosystem (architecture, app lifecycle, etc.).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional experience with SwiftUI is preferred, but a deep appreciation for building modern user interfaces is essential.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Swift Concurrency (async/await) for building responsive, performant applications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal communication skills and ability to iterate quickly with teammates, incorporating feedback and holding a high bar for quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with frameworks like Combine or Core Data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with the end-to-end App Store release process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">(Bonus Points) Knowledge of cryptography, secure enclave, or cellular technologies (eSIM, 4G, 5G).</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Compensation</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. <strong>Salary range for this role in New York, New York is $180,000 - $235,000 depending on experience and interview performance.</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our benefits include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stipends for</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Family-forming needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gender-affirming care</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Culture &amp; Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How to apply</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Click the link below to apply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT CAPE\n\nCape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.\n\nInstead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected and have privacy.\n\nWe didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.\n\nToday, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM\n\nAt Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nCape’s platform gives customers end-to-end control of their digital identity, optimizing for resiliency, privacy, and security at every turn. We’re transforming how customers sign up, use, and think about their mobile phones and the privacy implications associated with it. Customers are protected at every level of the communications stack – from the mobile device, through infrastructure, and to the core of the network itself.\n\nAs an iOS Engineer at Cape, your mission is to build the definitive application for private mobile communication. We don’t just white label an application and do the bare minimum for onboarding and collecting payment. The mobile application is the interface where users build trust with Cape and protect their digital lives. You will own the entire feature lifecycle—from architectural design to App Store launch - using Swift and SwiftUI to solve some of the hardest technical challenges in security and cryptography in order to secure personal information (PII), account data, and even voice & SMS traffic. In our tight-knit engineering team, you won't just build features; you will ship the product that makes our promise of privacy a reality.\n\nYour day-to-day will change, but everything you work on has a high impact. One day you could be pushing to deliver a new capability to prevent targeting of soldiers on the battlefield, the next you could be architecting a new system to prevent financial fraud via SIM swaps for everyday citizens.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL WORK ON\n\n - Take ownership of the mobile product lifecycle, from conceptualization, through design & development, all the way to launch.\n\n - Maintain high coding standards through the development of guidelines, active participation in code reviews, and fostering a culture of continuous improvement and knowledge sharing among your team.\n\n - Champion the security, performance, and stability of our applications. You will implement and oversee robust testing, monitoring, and release processes to guarantee a seamless and trustworthy user experience.\n\n - Actively improve user workflows by collaborating with cross-functional teams, ensuring seamless experiences across product boundaries and a cohesive user experience.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE VALUE\n\n - Proven ability to learn continuously, work independently, and make decisions with minimal supervision.\n\n - Experience brainstorming and iterating with product designers.\n\n - Ability to take a thoughtful, practical approach to problem-solving that considers tradeoffs and avoids over-engineering.\n\n - Skill and comfort working in a constantly evolving environment with dynamic objectives and iteration with users.\n\n - Ability to work collaboratively in teams of technical and non-technical individuals and understand how technical decisions impact the people who will use what you're building.\n\n - Understanding of cryptographic systems and how to design privacy conscious solutions.\n\n - Ability to learn new technology and concepts, even without in-depth experience.\n   \n   \n\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n - 4+ years of iOS software development experience.\n\n - Engineering background in Computer Science, Mathematics, Software Engineering, Physics or similar field.\n\n - Proficiency in Swift and a strong foundational understanding of the iOS ecosystem (architecture, app lifecycle, etc.).\n\n - Professional experience with SwiftUI is preferred, but a deep appreciation for building modern user interfaces is essential.\n\n - Experience with Swift Concurrency (async/await) for building responsive, performant applications.\n\n - Strong written and verbal communication skills and ability to iterate quickly with teammates, incorporating feedback and holding a high bar for quality.\n\n - Familiarity with frameworks like Combine or Core Data.\n\n - Hands-on experience with the end-to-end App Store release process.\n\n - (Bonus Points) Knowledge of cryptography, secure enclave, or cellular technologies (eSIM, 4G, 5G).\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nWe offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in New York, New York is $180,000 - $235,000 depending on experience and interview performance.\n\nOur benefits include:\n\n - 401(k) match\n\n - 100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents\n\n - 12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)\n\n - Stipends for\n   \n   - Family-forming needs\n   \n   - Gender-affirming care\n\n - Unlimited PTO\n\n\n\n\nOUR CULTURE & VALUES\n\n - We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.\n\n - We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.\n\n - We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.\n\n - We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nClick the link below to apply.\n\nWe reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.\n\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"c2b9c1b7-ae65-4e1a-928b-47360274a3ee","title":"Software Engineer, Android","department":"Engineering","team":"Mobile","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York, NY","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-09T19:43:13.233+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"450 Park Avenue South","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/c2b9c1b7-ae65-4e1a-928b-47360274a3ee","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/c2b9c1b7-ae65-4e1a-928b-47360274a3ee/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Cape</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected <em>and</em> have privacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Role</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape’s platform gives customers end-to-end control of their digital identity, optimizing for resiliency, privacy, and security at every turn. We’re transforming how customers sign up for, use, and think about their mobile phones—and the privacy implications associated with them. Customers are protected at every level of the communications stack—from the mobile device, through infrastructure, and to the core of the network itself.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Android Engineer at Cape, your mission is to build the definitive application for private mobile communication. We don’t just white-label an application and do the bare minimum for onboarding and collecting payment. The mobile application is the interface where users build trust with Cape and protect their digital lives. You will own the entire feature lifecycle—from architectural design to launch on both the Google Play Store and alternative, privacy-conscious app stores. Using Kotlin and Jetpack Compose, you will tackle some of the hardest technical challenges in security and cryptography in order to secure personal information (PII), account data, and even voice and SMS traffic. In our tight-knit engineering team, you won't just build features - you will ship the product that makes our promise of privacy a reality.<br /></p><h1><strong>What You'll Work On</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Take ownership of the mobile product lifecycle — from conceptualization, through design and development, all the way to launch.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain high coding standards by developing guidelines, actively participating in code reviews, and fostering a culture of continuous improvement and knowledge sharing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Champion the security, performance, and stability of our applications by implementing and overseeing robust testing, monitoring, and release processes to guarantee a seamless, trustworthy user experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actively improve user workflows by collaborating with cross-functional teams, ensuring seamless experiences across product boundaries and a cohesive user journey.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What We Value</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to learn continuously, work independently, and make decisions with minimal supervision.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A thoughtful, practical approach to problem-solving that considers tradeoffs and avoids over-engineering.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort working in a constantly evolving environment with dynamic objectives and frequent iteration with users.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to collaborate effectively with both technical and non-technical teammates, and an understanding of how technical decisions impact users.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to learn new technologies and concepts, even without prior in-depth experience.<br /></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Experience</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of Android software development experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in Computer Science, Mathematics, Software Engineering, Physics, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in Kotlin and a strong foundational understanding of the Android ecosystem (architecture, app lifecycle, concurrency, etc.).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional experience with Jetpack Compose is preferred, but a deep appreciation for building modern user interfaces is essential.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to iterate quickly with teammates, incorporate feedback, and maintain a high bar for quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience brainstorming and iterating with product designers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Android concurrency and storage frameworks such as Coroutines, Room, and DataStore.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with privacy-focused Android OSs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">(Bonus Points) Knowledge of cryptography, trusted execution environments and StrongBox, or cellular technologies (eSIM, 4G, 5G).</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Compensation</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. <strong>Salary range for this role in New York, New York is $180,000 - $235,000 depending on experience and interview performance.</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our benefits include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stipends for</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Family-forming needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gender-affirming care</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your day-to-day will vary, but everything you work on will have a high impact. One day, you could be delivering a new capability to prevent targeting of soldiers on the battlefield; the next, you could be architecting a system to prevent financial fraud via SIM swaps for everyday citizens.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Culture &amp; Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How to apply</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Click the link below to apply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT CAPE\n\nCape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.\n\nInstead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected and have privacy.\n\nWe didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.\n\nToday, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM\n\nAt Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nCape’s platform gives customers end-to-end control of their digital identity, optimizing for resiliency, privacy, and security at every turn. We’re transforming how customers sign up for, use, and think about their mobile phones—and the privacy implications associated with them. Customers are protected at every level of the communications stack—from the mobile device, through infrastructure, and to the core of the network itself.\n\nAs an Android Engineer at Cape, your mission is to build the definitive application for private mobile communication. We don’t just white-label an application and do the bare minimum for onboarding and collecting payment. The mobile application is the interface where users build trust with Cape and protect their digital lives. You will own the entire feature lifecycle—from architectural design to launch on both the Google Play Store and alternative, privacy-conscious app stores. Using Kotlin and Jetpack Compose, you will tackle some of the hardest technical challenges in security and cryptography in order to secure personal information (PII), account data, and even voice and SMS traffic. In our tight-knit engineering team, you won't just build features - you will ship the product that makes our promise of privacy a reality.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL WORK ON\n\n - Take ownership of the mobile product lifecycle — from conceptualization, through design and development, all the way to launch.\n\n - Maintain high coding standards by developing guidelines, actively participating in code reviews, and fostering a culture of continuous improvement and knowledge sharing.\n\n - Champion the security, performance, and stability of our applications by implementing and overseeing robust testing, monitoring, and release processes to guarantee a seamless, trustworthy user experience.\n\n - Actively improve user workflows by collaborating with cross-functional teams, ensuring seamless experiences across product boundaries and a cohesive user journey.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE VALUE\n\n - Proven ability to learn continuously, work independently, and make decisions with minimal supervision.\n\n - A thoughtful, practical approach to problem-solving that considers tradeoffs and avoids over-engineering.\n\n - Comfort working in a constantly evolving environment with dynamic objectives and frequent iteration with users.\n\n - Ability to collaborate effectively with both technical and non-technical teammates, and an understanding of how technical decisions impact users.\n\n - Ability to learn new technologies and concepts, even without prior in-depth experience.\n   \n\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n - 4+ years of Android software development experience.\n\n - Background in Computer Science, Mathematics, Software Engineering, Physics, or a related field.\n\n - Proficiency in Kotlin and a strong foundational understanding of the Android ecosystem (architecture, app lifecycle, concurrency, etc.).\n\n - Professional experience with Jetpack Compose is preferred, but a deep appreciation for building modern user interfaces is essential.\n\n - Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to iterate quickly with teammates, incorporate feedback, and maintain a high bar for quality.\n\n - Experience brainstorming and iterating with product designers.\n\n - Experience with Android concurrency and storage frameworks such as Coroutines, Room, and DataStore.\n\n - Familiarity with privacy-focused Android OSs.\n\n - (Bonus Points) Knowledge of cryptography, trusted execution environments and StrongBox, or cellular technologies (eSIM, 4G, 5G).\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nWe offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in New York, New York is $180,000 - $235,000 depending on experience and interview performance.\n\nOur benefits include:\n\n - 401(k) match\n\n - 100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents\n\n - 12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)\n\n - Stipends for\n   \n   - Family-forming needs\n   \n   - Gender-affirming care\n\n - Unlimited PTO\n\nYour day-to-day will vary, but everything you work on will have a high impact. One day, you could be delivering a new capability to prevent targeting of soldiers on the battlefield; the next, you could be architecting a system to prevent financial fraud via SIM swaps for everyday citizens.\n\n\n\n\nOUR CULTURE & VALUES\n\n - We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.\n\n - We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.\n\n - We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.\n\n - We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nClick the link below to apply.\n\nWe reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.\n\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"3f6ca5b3-eed4-4b0c-b5d2-5ec7f45aae26","title":"Head of Forward Deployed Engineering","department":"Engineering","team":"FDE","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York, NY","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Arlington, VA","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Virginia","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Arlington"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-04-02T22:51:36.150+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"450 Park Avenue South","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/3f6ca5b3-eed4-4b0c-b5d2-5ec7f45aae26","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/3f6ca5b3-eed4-4b0c-b5d2-5ec7f45aae26/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Cape</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected <em>and</em> have privacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>The Problem</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The commercial cellular network represents trillions of dollars in private investment worldwide. It is performant, highly available, near ubiquitous, and the spec is mature and well understood. It’s the perfect transport layer for government use cases, if only they could trust the network. But they cannot: that infrastructure is easily disrupted and surveilled, and existing solutions are typically clunky, proprietary, and fail at the first sign of a contested RF environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape started at first principles to build a secure network architecture that operates through assumed compromised physical infrastructure. Now we need to solve operational capabilities at scale. How do we provide security-first, resilient communications for operators at the tactical edge? How do we ensure connectivity without compromise when the backhaul is being actively jammed, intercepted, or physically severed?</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are moving from validated technology to <strong>mission-critical infrastructure</strong> that works in contested environments when failure is not an option. Leading this team of engineers is a high stakes, critical role and will be deeply rewarding for the right person.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>The Role</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape’s platform gives customers end-to-end control of their digital identity, even as they connect to untrusted networks, optimizing for resiliency, privacy, and security at every turn. As the Head of Federal Engineering, you will gain rare insight into the world’s most challenging environments. You will own the technical execution of the federal business, partnering with Business Development and Product to bridge the gap between our core technology and the specific, demanding requirements of our government partners.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will cultivate a high-performing technical team, providing the mentorship needed to deliver outcomes in highly regulated spaces. Your charge is to grow the business and empower your engineers to work autonomously in remote locations, making great technical decisions to build the most overlooked yet critical components of modern Command and Control (C2)--the transport layer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What You'll Work On</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect and execute the technical vision for our federal engineering organization, building the secure, resilient, and scalable network and platform that our nation's most critical missions depend on. Your leadership will directly translate our privacy-first ethos into capabilities that protect and empower those in public service.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, mentor, and inspire a world-class team of engineers dedicated to solving the nation's toughest Command and Control challenges. You will foster a culture of innovation, collaboration, and unwavering integrity, empowering your team to deliver solutions that meet the highest standards of excellence and impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the key technical partner to our federal customers, translating their complex mission requirements into tangible, deployed solutions. You will build and nurture deep relationships, ensuring that we are not just a vendor, but a trusted partner in advancing national security and public trust.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Take complete ownership and serve as the technical owner for our federal customers. You will ensure that our engineering practices, security protocols, and delivery timelines set a new standard for what is possible in government technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Steer our engagement with the unique challenges and opportunities of the federal landscape. You will be the bridge between our core technology and the specific, demanding requirements of our government partners, ensuring our solutions are always at the vanguard of innovation and mission-ready.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What We Value</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to learn continuously, work independently, and make decisions with minimal supervision.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A belief that the best leaders empower their teams to achieve the impossible. You are a mentor and a force-multiplier, dedicated to growing the next generation of engineering leaders and fostering a culture where every individual can do their best work in service of the mission.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ability to take a thoughtful, practical approach to problem-solving that considers tradeoffs and avoids over-engineering.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Skill and comfort working in a constantly evolving environment with dynamic objectives and iteration with users.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ability to work collaboratively in teams of technical and non-technical individuals and understand how technical decisions impact the customer.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of cryptographic systems and how to design privacy conscious solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ability to learn new technology and concepts, even without in-depth experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ability to balance a forward-looking vision with the concrete realities of government requirements and constraints. You find creative yet practical paths to deploy modern technology within highly regulated environments, ensuring solutions are not just innovative, but also accreditable and effective.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are more than a technical leader; you are a diplomat and a strategist. You excel at building strong, collaborative relationships with government partners and internal stakeholders, translating mission needs into technical reality with clarity and conviction.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Experience</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engineering background in Computer Science, Mathematics, Computer Engineering, Physics or similar field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated success leading engineering teams that have built, deployed, and sustained software solutions for U.S. government, defense, or intelligence community customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of modern software architecture, particularly for secure, scalable, and distributed systems. Experience with both cloud (e.g., AWS GovCloud, Azure Government) as well as air-gapped environments, and familiarity with federal security compliance standards (e.g., FedRAMP, RMF, STIGs) is helpful.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to define a technical strategy and execute against it, aligning engineering efforts with both customer mission objectives and broader business goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ability to articulate complex technical concepts with authority and clarity to a wide range of audiences, from your own engineers to senior government officials and non-technical stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An active U.S. Top Secret (TS) security clearance is strongly preferred. At a minimum, you must have the ability to obtain and maintain a U.S. security clearance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Compensation</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive compensation that is <strong>geo-adjusted</strong> based on <strong>your location</strong>, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in New York, New York is $200,000-$275,000 depending on experience and interview performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our benefits include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stipends for</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Family-forming needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gender-affirming care</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Culture &amp; Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How to apply</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Click the link below to apply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT CAPE\n\nCape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.\n\nInstead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected and have privacy.\n\nWe didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.\n\nToday, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM\n\nAt Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.\n\n\n\n\nTHE PROBLEM\n\nThe commercial cellular network represents trillions of dollars in private investment worldwide. It is performant, highly available, near ubiquitous, and the spec is mature and well understood. It’s the perfect transport layer for government use cases, if only they could trust the network. But they cannot: that infrastructure is easily disrupted and surveilled, and existing solutions are typically clunky, proprietary, and fail at the first sign of a contested RF environment.\n\nCape started at first principles to build a secure network architecture that operates through assumed compromised physical infrastructure. Now we need to solve operational capabilities at scale. How do we provide security-first, resilient communications for operators at the tactical edge? How do we ensure connectivity without compromise when the backhaul is being actively jammed, intercepted, or physically severed?\n\nWe are moving from validated technology to mission-critical infrastructure that works in contested environments when failure is not an option. Leading this team of engineers is a high stakes, critical role and will be deeply rewarding for the right person.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nCape’s platform gives customers end-to-end control of their digital identity, even as they connect to untrusted networks, optimizing for resiliency, privacy, and security at every turn. As the Head of Federal Engineering, you will gain rare insight into the world’s most challenging environments. You will own the technical execution of the federal business, partnering with Business Development and Product to bridge the gap between our core technology and the specific, demanding requirements of our government partners.\n\nYou will cultivate a high-performing technical team, providing the mentorship needed to deliver outcomes in highly regulated spaces. Your charge is to grow the business and empower your engineers to work autonomously in remote locations, making great technical decisions to build the most overlooked yet critical components of modern Command and Control (C2)--the transport layer.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL WORK ON\n\n - Architect and execute the technical vision for our federal engineering organization, building the secure, resilient, and scalable network and platform that our nation's most critical missions depend on. Your leadership will directly translate our privacy-first ethos into capabilities that protect and empower those in public service.\n\n - Lead, mentor, and inspire a world-class team of engineers dedicated to solving the nation's toughest Command and Control challenges. You will foster a culture of innovation, collaboration, and unwavering integrity, empowering your team to deliver solutions that meet the highest standards of excellence and impact.\n\n - Serve as the key technical partner to our federal customers, translating their complex mission requirements into tangible, deployed solutions. You will build and nurture deep relationships, ensuring that we are not just a vendor, but a trusted partner in advancing national security and public trust.\n\n - Take complete ownership and serve as the technical owner for our federal customers. You will ensure that our engineering practices, security protocols, and delivery timelines set a new standard for what is possible in government technology.\n\n - Steer our engagement with the unique challenges and opportunities of the federal landscape. You will be the bridge between our core technology and the specific, demanding requirements of our government partners, ensuring our solutions are always at the vanguard of innovation and mission-ready.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE VALUE\n\n - Proven ability to learn continuously, work independently, and make decisions with minimal supervision.\n\n - A belief that the best leaders empower their teams to achieve the impossible. You are a mentor and a force-multiplier, dedicated to growing the next generation of engineering leaders and fostering a culture where every individual can do their best work in service of the mission.\n\n - The ability to take a thoughtful, practical approach to problem-solving that considers tradeoffs and avoids over-engineering.\n\n - Skill and comfort working in a constantly evolving environment with dynamic objectives and iteration with users.\n\n - The ability to work collaboratively in teams of technical and non-technical individuals and understand how technical decisions impact the customer.\n\n - Understanding of cryptographic systems and how to design privacy conscious solutions.\n\n - The ability to learn new technology and concepts, even without in-depth experience.\n\n - The ability to balance a forward-looking vision with the concrete realities of government requirements and constraints. You find creative yet practical paths to deploy modern technology within highly regulated environments, ensuring solutions are not just innovative, but also accreditable and effective.\n\n - You are more than a technical leader; you are a diplomat and a strategist. You excel at building strong, collaborative relationships with government partners and internal stakeholders, translating mission needs into technical reality with clarity and conviction.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n - Engineering background in Computer Science, Mathematics, Computer Engineering, Physics or similar field.\n\n - Demonstrated success leading engineering teams that have built, deployed, and sustained software solutions for U.S. government, defense, or intelligence community customers.\n\n - Understanding of modern software architecture, particularly for secure, scalable, and distributed systems. Experience with both cloud (e.g., AWS GovCloud, Azure Government) as well as air-gapped environments, and familiarity with federal security compliance standards (e.g., FedRAMP, RMF, STIGs) is helpful.\n\n - Proven ability to define a technical strategy and execute against it, aligning engineering efforts with both customer mission objectives and broader business goals.\n\n - The ability to articulate complex technical concepts with authority and clarity to a wide range of audiences, from your own engineers to senior government officials and non-technical stakeholders.\n\n - An active U.S. Top Secret (TS) security clearance is strongly preferred. At a minimum, you must have the ability to obtain and maintain a U.S. security clearance.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nWe offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in New York, New York is $200,000-$275,000 depending on experience and interview performance.\n\nOur benefits include:\n\n - 401(k) match\n\n - 100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents\n\n - 12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)\n\n - Stipends for\n   \n   - Family-forming needs\n   \n   - Gender-affirming care\n\n\n\n\nOUR CULTURE & VALUES\n\n - We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.\n\n - We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.\n\n - We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.\n\n - We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nClick the link below to apply.\n\nWe reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.\n\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"4c39666a-92c9-40fa-9d63-fd591aaf64ff","title":"Software Engineer, Infrastructure","department":"Engineering","team":"SRE","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote USA","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Arlington, VA","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Virginia","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Arlington"}}},{"location":"New York, NY","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"450 Park Avenue South","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}}}],"publishedAt":"2025-10-20T19:30:19.441+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/4c39666a-92c9-40fa-9d63-fd591aaf64ff","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/4c39666a-92c9-40fa-9d63-fd591aaf64ff/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Cape</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected <em>and</em> have privacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>The Role</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To join our team, you should be excited to:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Dive into a well-funded but early-stage startup. We’re in a scrappy phase, be comfortable getting a little uncomfortable.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reclaim some of the personal privacy we have all sacrificed as smartphone adoption has grown.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flex your technical skills on hard, important problems with serious implications for consumer privacy and national security.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Push the envelope - we are using new technology in novel ways.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work on greenfield problems. Starting new projects from the ground up. Shaping the stack, practices, and getting the opportunity to try new tools and technologies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work in person! There are no facetime requirements or set hours here, and we all take work from home days. But our default work location is our DC or NY office, and we enjoy the informal culture and serendipity that in-person work enables.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re offering competitive salary, benefits, and equity with early-stage upside.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What You'll Work On</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be responsible for the full lifecycle development of our privacy-focused telecommunications and deployment infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build, integrate, and maintain our instrumentation and monitoring infrastructure and tooling for improving the reliability, availability, and performance of our system.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help solve issues proactively before they become issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build new or integrate with existing telecommunications infrastructure and components.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the technical accreditation and compliance process end-to-end for FedRamp.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Shape and influence what great software engineering practices look like.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Balance short term critical business needs with long term product vision and roadmap.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Experience</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Although we list out what we generally look for, we are likely missing other attributes and skills that you have that could make you a great fit, but are not currently listed. It doesn’t hurt to take a chance and apply!</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of software engineering or SRE experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong familiarity with AWS.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in Golang, Rust, Java/Kotlin, Python, or similar language.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with building, deploying, and using monitoring infrastructure &amp; tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing, building, and delivering high availability systems and infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passion for privacy and national security.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A desire to work on software that has real-world impact.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Azure and/or GCP in addition to AWS.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with mobile telecommunications technologies such as IP media subsystem (IMS), 4G/5G mobile core network functions, and/or multimedia protocols.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing redundant, high availability multi-site deployments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience organizing documentation to support accreditation processes such as FedRamp and ATOs.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Compensation</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive compensation that is <strong>geo-adjusted</strong> based on <strong>your location</strong>, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in New York, New York is $180,000-$230,000 depending on experience and interview performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our benefits include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stipends for</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Family-forming needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gender-affirming care</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Culture &amp; Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How to apply</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Click the link below to apply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT CAPE\n\nCape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.\n\nInstead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected and have privacy.\n\nWe didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.\n\nToday, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM\n\nAt Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nTo join our team, you should be excited to:\n\n - Dive into a well-funded but early-stage startup. We’re in a scrappy phase, be comfortable getting a little uncomfortable.\n\n - Reclaim some of the personal privacy we have all sacrificed as smartphone adoption has grown.\n\n - Flex your technical skills on hard, important problems with serious implications for consumer privacy and national security.\n\n - Push the envelope - we are using new technology in novel ways.\n\n - Work on greenfield problems. Starting new projects from the ground up. Shaping the stack, practices, and getting the opportunity to try new tools and technologies.\n\n - Work in person! There are no facetime requirements or set hours here, and we all take work from home days. But our default work location is our DC or NY office, and we enjoy the informal culture and serendipity that in-person work enables.\n\nWe’re offering competitive salary, benefits, and equity with early-stage upside.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL WORK ON\n\n - Be responsible for the full lifecycle development of our privacy-focused telecommunications and deployment infrastructure.\n\n - Build, integrate, and maintain our instrumentation and monitoring infrastructure and tooling for improving the reliability, availability, and performance of our system.\n\n - Help solve issues proactively before they become issues.\n\n - Build new or integrate with existing telecommunications infrastructure and components.\n\n - Own the technical accreditation and compliance process end-to-end for FedRamp.\n\n - Shape and influence what great software engineering practices look like.\n\n - Balance short term critical business needs with long term product vision and roadmap.\n\n\n\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\nAlthough we list out what we generally look for, we are likely missing other attributes and skills that you have that could make you a great fit, but are not currently listed. It doesn’t hurt to take a chance and apply!\n\n - 4+ years of software engineering or SRE experience.\n\n - Strong familiarity with AWS.\n\n - Fluency in Golang, Rust, Java/Kotlin, Python, or similar language.\n\n - Experience with building, deploying, and using monitoring infrastructure & tools.\n\n - Experience designing, building, and delivering high availability systems and infrastructure.\n\n - Passion for privacy and national security.\n\n - A desire to work on software that has real-world impact.\n\n\n\nNice to have\n\n - Familiarity with Azure and/or GCP in addition to AWS.\n\n - Familiarity with mobile telecommunications technologies such as IP media subsystem (IMS), 4G/5G mobile core network functions, and/or multimedia protocols.\n\n - Experience managing redundant, high availability multi-site deployments.\n\n - Experience organizing documentation to support accreditation processes such as FedRamp and ATOs.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nWe offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in New York, New York is $180,000-$230,000 depending on experience and interview performance.\n\nOur benefits include:\n\n - 401(k) match\n\n - 100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents\n\n - 12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)\n\n - Stipends for\n   \n   - Family-forming needs\n   \n   - Gender-affirming care\n\n - Unlimited PTO\n\n\n\n\nOUR CULTURE & VALUES\n\n - We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.\n\n - We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.\n\n - We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.\n\n - We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nClick the link below to apply.\n\nWe reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.\n\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"991713f3-ea5b-4887-8d94-41df776a1a6f","title":"Full Stack Software Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Full Stack","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York, NY","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-15T16:14:46.570+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"450 Park Avenue South","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/991713f3-ea5b-4887-8d94-41df776a1a6f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/991713f3-ea5b-4887-8d94-41df776a1a6f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Cape</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected <em>and</em> have privacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>The Role</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape’s platform gives customers end-to-end control of their digital identity, optimizing for resiliency, privacy, and security at every turn. We’re transforming how customers sign up, use, and think about their mobile phones and the privacy implications associated with it. Customers are protected at every level of the communications stack – from the mobile device, through contested infrastructure, to the core of the network itself.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a<strong> </strong>Full Stack Software Engineer at Cape, your mission is to provide connectivity without compromise. Your charge is to build a system that enables resilient, global connectivity with a security &amp; privacy first mind-set that separates our users from the legacy telecom ecosystem. This includes everything from building a best-in-class signaling firewall to identify &amp; mitigate malicious signaling attacks that compromise users' most personal communications, to detection of fake base-stations (cell-site simulators), to detecting and preventing SPAM &amp; Smishing campaigns, and being transparent and alerting users when they may be actively targeted by hackers or nation states. Fluency across the full stack allows you to have even more ownership and agency to lead this charge.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re hiring engineers who are passionate about solving real-world problems, personal privacy, and empowering peers to be autonomous. If you’re motivated to develop reliable, highly performant, and scalable systems, and to design robust APIs and primitives, this role offers the opportunity to make a significant impact on our products and the people who use them. Your day-to-day will constantly change and be filled with ambiguity, but everything you work on has a high impact.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Work On</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build beautiful, responsive and reliable websites and landing pages.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work in Figma, and translate designs into code.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain high coding standards through the development of guidelines, active participation in code reviews, and fostering a culture of continuous improvement and knowledge sharing among your team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Champion the security, performance, and stability of our web applications. You will implement and oversee robust testing, monitoring, and release processes to guarantee a seamless and trustworthy user experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actively improve user workflows by collaborating with cross-functional teams, ensuring seamless experiences across product boundaries and a cohesive user experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build reliable, performant, and scalable systems that enable other product teams to build robust web applications without requiring deep domain expertise in the underlying infrastructure.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What We Value</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to learn continuously, work independently, and make decisions with minimal supervision.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience brainstorming and iterating with product designers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High ownership and the drive to take a problem from ideation to production independently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to take a thoughtful, practical approach to problem-solving that considers tradeoffs and avoids over-engineering.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Skill and comfort working in a constantly evolving environment with dynamic objectives and iteration with users.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work collaboratively in teams of technical and non-technical individuals and understand how technical decisions impact the people who will use what you're building.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of cryptographic systems and how to design privacy conscious solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to learn new technology and concepts, even without in-depth experience.</p></li></ul><h1><br /><strong>Experience</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of full stack software engineering experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engineering background in Computer Science, Mathematics, Software Engineering, Physics or similar field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience crafting complex user experiences (UX) with a strong intuition for good design and usability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional coding skills regardless of framework or stack, especially with TypeScript React (or similar frontend programming language and framework) and Go (or similar backend programming language).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with data structures, loading patterns, web frameworks, and other technical tools and concepts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal communication skills and ability to iterate quickly with teammates, incorporating feedback and holding a high bar for quality.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Compensation</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive compensation that is <strong>geo-adjusted</strong> based on <strong>your location</strong>, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in New York, New York is $220,000-$250,000 depending on experience and interview performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our benefits include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stipends for</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Family-forming needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gender-affirming care</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Culture &amp; Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How to apply</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Click the link below to apply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT CAPE\n\nCape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.\n\nInstead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected and have privacy.\n\nWe didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.\n\nToday, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM\n\nAt Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nCape’s platform gives customers end-to-end control of their digital identity, optimizing for resiliency, privacy, and security at every turn. We’re transforming how customers sign up, use, and think about their mobile phones and the privacy implications associated with it. Customers are protected at every level of the communications stack – from the mobile device, through contested infrastructure, to the core of the network itself.\n\nAs a Full Stack Software Engineer at Cape, your mission is to provide connectivity without compromise. Your charge is to build a system that enables resilient, global connectivity with a security & privacy first mind-set that separates our users from the legacy telecom ecosystem. This includes everything from building a best-in-class signaling firewall to identify & mitigate malicious signaling attacks that compromise users' most personal communications, to detection of fake base-stations (cell-site simulators), to detecting and preventing SPAM & Smishing campaigns, and being transparent and alerting users when they may be actively targeted by hackers or nation states. Fluency across the full stack allows you to have even more ownership and agency to lead this charge.\n\nWe’re hiring engineers who are passionate about solving real-world problems, personal privacy, and empowering peers to be autonomous. If you’re motivated to develop reliable, highly performant, and scalable systems, and to design robust APIs and primitives, this role offers the opportunity to make a significant impact on our products and the people who use them. Your day-to-day will constantly change and be filled with ambiguity, but everything you work on has a high impact.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL WORK ON\n\n - Build beautiful, responsive and reliable websites and landing pages.\n\n - Work in Figma, and translate designs into code.\n\n - Maintain high coding standards through the development of guidelines, active participation in code reviews, and fostering a culture of continuous improvement and knowledge sharing among your team.\n\n - Champion the security, performance, and stability of our web applications. You will implement and oversee robust testing, monitoring, and release processes to guarantee a seamless and trustworthy user experience.\n\n - Actively improve user workflows by collaborating with cross-functional teams, ensuring seamless experiences across product boundaries and a cohesive user experience.\n\n - Build reliable, performant, and scalable systems that enable other product teams to build robust web applications without requiring deep domain expertise in the underlying infrastructure.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE VALUE\n\n - Proven ability to learn continuously, work independently, and make decisions with minimal supervision.\n\n - Experience brainstorming and iterating with product designers.\n\n - High ownership and the drive to take a problem from ideation to production independently.\n\n - Ability to take a thoughtful, practical approach to problem-solving that considers tradeoffs and avoids over-engineering.\n\n - Skill and comfort working in a constantly evolving environment with dynamic objectives and iteration with users.\n\n - Ability to work collaboratively in teams of technical and non-technical individuals and understand how technical decisions impact the people who will use what you're building.\n\n - Understanding of cryptographic systems and how to design privacy conscious solutions.\n\n - Ability to learn new technology and concepts, even without in-depth experience.\n\n\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n - 4+ years of full stack software engineering experience.\n\n - Engineering background in Computer Science, Mathematics, Software Engineering, Physics or similar field.\n\n - Experience crafting complex user experiences (UX) with a strong intuition for good design and usability.\n\n - Exceptional coding skills regardless of framework or stack, especially with TypeScript React (or similar frontend programming language and framework) and Go (or similar backend programming language).\n\n - Familiarity with data structures, loading patterns, web frameworks, and other technical tools and concepts.\n\n - Strong written and verbal communication skills and ability to iterate quickly with teammates, incorporating feedback and holding a high bar for quality.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nWe offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in New York, New York is $220,000-$250,000 depending on experience and interview performance.\n\nOur benefits include:\n\n - 401(k) match\n\n - 100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents\n\n - 12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)\n\n - Stipends for\n   \n   - Family-forming needs\n   \n   - Gender-affirming care\n\n\n\n\nOUR CULTURE & VALUES\n\n - We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.\n\n - We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.\n\n - We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.\n\n - We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nClick the link below to apply.\n\nWe reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.\n\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"6311bc82-157b-48f5-9b05-a4bf6c2d0b3f","title":"Security Engineer, Product Security","department":"Security","team":"Security Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote USA","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-06T21:47:12.265+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/6311bc82-157b-48f5-9b05-a4bf6c2d0b3f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/6311bc82-157b-48f5-9b05-a4bf6c2d0b3f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Cape</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected <em>and</em> have privacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>The Role</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are seeking an experienced Security Engineer with a specialization in product security to join our team. As a strategic partner, you will make an immediate impact by leveraging your expertise in cloud and application security. This role is pivotal in reducing risk across our AWS cloud environments, mobile core infrastructure, and mobile applications. You will be responsible for designing, implementing, and that comply with regulatory standards, enhance internal processes, and minimize data security risks. Through developing ongoing security strategies and technologies, you will support the organization's business objectives and daily operations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What You'll Work On</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, implement, and manage robust security controls and policies within AWS, focusing on the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of data and services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform comprehensive security assessments of our cloud environments to identify vulnerabilities, assess risks, and recommend actionable mitigation strategies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the integration of security practices into the DevOps lifecycle, promoting secure development, deployment, and operational processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Utilize and optimize AWS security tools (such as Amazon GuardDuty, Amazon Inspector, AWS IAM, AWS KMS, AWS WAF, and AWS Shield) and explore third-party solutions to bolster our security posture.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist in running and address findings from penetration tests and security audits, and ensuring prompt and effective remediation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay informed about the latest security threats, vulnerabilities, and compliance mandates affecting cloud environments, provide strategic guidance on technologies and best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide expert mentorship to junior security team members and engineers across the company, to foster an organizational culture of security awareness and continuous improvement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with stakeholders to integrate security requirements effectively into engineering projects and broader business initiatives.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Experience</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Security, or a related field (or equivalent experience), Advanced degrees or certifications (e.g., CISSP, AWS Certified Security Specialty) are advantageous.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A minimum of 5 years of experience in information security, with at least 3 years concentrated on cloud security within AWS environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of AWS architecture, security services, and best practices for securing cloud applications and data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in using infrastructure as code (IaC) tools (like Terraform or AWS CloudFormation) and in automating security tasks within AWS.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Skilled in scripting languages (Python, TypeScript, Go) for the automation of security tasks and the integration of security tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with containerization and microservices, particularly in securing stacks using these technologies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid knowledge of network security, encryption technologies, and secure coding practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent analytical skills for identifying and mitigating complex security vulnerabilities and risks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and leadership abilities, capable of working collaboratively across teams and effectively conveying technical information to non-technical stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organized and able to manage multiple priorities in a dynamic, fast-paced environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Competencies</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Role competencies</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Security Expertise:</strong> Experience finding and resolving security issues and vulnerabilities in code. Bug Bounty programs. Secure by design principals and working with engineers during design time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Analytical:</strong> Collects data and information; uses critical thinking to solve problems and make sound decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaboration &amp; Teamwork:</strong> Builds partnerships with others to reach common goals. Able to share credit with coworkers, display enthusiasm and promote a friendly group working environment. Works closely with other departments as necessary, supports group decisions and solicits opinions from coworkers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Communication:</strong> Presents information through verbal and written communication; reads and interprets complex information; listens well. Develops and delivers multi-mode communications that convey clear understanding of unique audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Decision-Making:</strong> Acts quickly to solve problems and exercises good judgment by making sound and well-informed decisions. Perceives the impact and implications of decisions; makes effective and timely decisions, even when data is limited.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Dependability/Self-Management:</strong> Possesses the personal discipline and diligence necessary to keep commitments and to complete tasks. Is accountable for actions and outcomes. Makes effort to improve situations without explicit instructions; a self-starter who consciously manages his/her own time and resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Customer Centric</strong>: Values the importance of delivering high quality, innovative service to employees; understands the needs of the client; responds promptly and is accessible to them; follows through on commitments in a timely manner; maintains positive, long-term working relationships; assumes ownership of process issues and takes appropriate steps to mitigate problems. Gets consistently high feedback from stakeholders. Raises hand to help.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexibility / adaptability</strong>: Adjusts quickly to changing priorities, conditions, and challenges. Copes effectively with complexity and change. Is comfortable navigating ambiguity. Can handle business changes with ease and with a lack of frustration or feeling of defeat. Feels comfortable dealing with limited unknowns in an area they are well versed in.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Planning &amp; Organization:</strong> Manages multiple projects, determines project urgency in a meaningful and practical way, uses goals to guide actions, creates detailed action plans, and organizes tasks.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Cape-specific competencies</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Do Excellent Work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respect The Opportunity (each other, the user)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Overshare</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bias Towards Action</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Compensation</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive compensation that is <strong>geo-adjusted</strong> based on <strong>your location</strong>, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in New York, New York is $200,000-$255,000 depending on experience and interview performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our benefits include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stipends for</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Family-forming needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gender-affirming care</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Culture &amp; Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How to apply</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Click the link below to apply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT CAPE\n\nCape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.\n\nInstead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected and have privacy.\n\nWe didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.\n\nToday, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM\n\nAt Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nWe are seeking an experienced Security Engineer with a specialization in product security to join our team. As a strategic partner, you will make an immediate impact by leveraging your expertise in cloud and application security. This role is pivotal in reducing risk across our AWS cloud environments, mobile core infrastructure, and mobile applications. You will be responsible for designing, implementing, and that comply with regulatory standards, enhance internal processes, and minimize data security risks. Through developing ongoing security strategies and technologies, you will support the organization's business objectives and daily operations.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL WORK ON\n\n - Design, implement, and manage robust security controls and policies within AWS, focusing on the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of data and services.\n\n - Perform comprehensive security assessments of our cloud environments to identify vulnerabilities, assess risks, and recommend actionable mitigation strategies.\n\n - Lead the integration of security practices into the DevOps lifecycle, promoting secure development, deployment, and operational processes.\n\n - Utilize and optimize AWS security tools (such as Amazon GuardDuty, Amazon Inspector, AWS IAM, AWS KMS, AWS WAF, and AWS Shield) and explore third-party solutions to bolster our security posture.\n\n - Assist in running and address findings from penetration tests and security audits, and ensuring prompt and effective remediation.\n\n - Stay informed about the latest security threats, vulnerabilities, and compliance mandates affecting cloud environments, provide strategic guidance on technologies and best practices.\n\n - Provide expert mentorship to junior security team members and engineers across the company, to foster an organizational culture of security awareness and continuous improvement.\n\n - Collaborate with stakeholders to integrate security requirements effectively into engineering projects and broader business initiatives.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n - Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Security, or a related field (or equivalent experience), Advanced degrees or certifications (e.g., CISSP, AWS Certified Security Specialty) are advantageous.\n\n - A minimum of 5 years of experience in information security, with at least 3 years concentrated on cloud security within AWS environments.\n\n - Deep understanding of AWS architecture, security services, and best practices for securing cloud applications and data.\n\n - Proficiency in using infrastructure as code (IaC) tools (like Terraform or AWS CloudFormation) and in automating security tasks within AWS.\n\n - Skilled in scripting languages (Python, TypeScript, Go) for the automation of security tasks and the integration of security tools.\n\n - Familiarity with containerization and microservices, particularly in securing stacks using these technologies.\n\n - Solid knowledge of network security, encryption technologies, and secure coding practices.\n\n - Excellent analytical skills for identifying and mitigating complex security vulnerabilities and risks.\n\n - Strong communication and leadership abilities, capable of working collaboratively across teams and effectively conveying technical information to non-technical stakeholders.\n\n - Organized and able to manage multiple priorities in a dynamic, fast-paced environment.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPETENCIES\n\nRole competencies\n\n - Security Expertise: Experience finding and resolving security issues and vulnerabilities in code. Bug Bounty programs. Secure by design principals and working with engineers during design time.\n\n - Analytical: Collects data and information; uses critical thinking to solve problems and make sound decisions.\n\n - Collaboration & Teamwork: Builds partnerships with others to reach common goals. Able to share credit with coworkers, display enthusiasm and promote a friendly group working environment. Works closely with other departments as necessary, supports group decisions and solicits opinions from coworkers.\n\n - Communication: Presents information through verbal and written communication; reads and interprets complex information; listens well. Develops and delivers multi-mode communications that convey clear understanding of unique audiences.\n\n - Decision-Making: Acts quickly to solve problems and exercises good judgment by making sound and well-informed decisions. Perceives the impact and implications of decisions; makes effective and timely decisions, even when data is limited.\n\n - Dependability/Self-Management: Possesses the personal discipline and diligence necessary to keep commitments and to complete tasks. Is accountable for actions and outcomes. Makes effort to improve situations without explicit instructions; a self-starter who consciously manages his/her own time and resources.\n\n - Customer Centric: Values the importance of delivering high quality, innovative service to employees; understands the needs of the client; responds promptly and is accessible to them; follows through on commitments in a timely manner; maintains positive, long-term working relationships; assumes ownership of process issues and takes appropriate steps to mitigate problems. Gets consistently high feedback from stakeholders. Raises hand to help.\n\n - Flexibility / adaptability: Adjusts quickly to changing priorities, conditions, and challenges. Copes effectively with complexity and change. Is comfortable navigating ambiguity. Can handle business changes with ease and with a lack of frustration or feeling of defeat. Feels comfortable dealing with limited unknowns in an area they are well versed in.\n\n - Planning & Organization: Manages multiple projects, determines project urgency in a meaningful and practical way, uses goals to guide actions, creates detailed action plans, and organizes tasks.\n\nCape-specific competencies\n\n - Do Excellent Work\n\n - Respect The Opportunity (each other, the user)\n\n - Overshare\n\n - Bias Towards Action\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nWe offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in New York, New York is $200,000-$255,000 depending on experience and interview performance.\n\nOur benefits include:\n\n - 401(k) match\n\n - 100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents\n\n - 12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)\n\n - Stipends for\n   \n   - Family-forming needs\n   \n   - Gender-affirming care\n\n - Unlimited PTO\n\n\n\n\nOUR CULTURE & VALUES\n\n - We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.\n\n - We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.\n\n - We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.\n\n - We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nClick the link below to apply.\n\nWe reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.\n\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"8b5eb0b3-b00b-47f9-afa6-de95a16f8f7a","title":"Technical Program Manager, Product & Engineering","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York, NY","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-13T22:21:24.989+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"450 Park Avenue South","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/8b5eb0b3-b00b-47f9-afa6-de95a16f8f7a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/8b5eb0b3-b00b-47f9-afa6-de95a16f8f7a/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Cape</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected <em>and</em> have privacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>The Role</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape has never had a Technical Program Manager, which means our engineering teams are moving fast on some of the hardest problems in telecom without the connective tissue to move even faster. Tickets go untracked, standups happen inconsistently, priorities blur across teams, and brilliant engineers spend more time untangling processes than solving problems. You'll be the first person to fix that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a builder's role, there's no playbook to inherit. You will design the systems, rituals, and rhythms our teams need from scratch, and prove their value fast enough that other teams start asking for you. You'll need to earn trust by going deep enough on the technology that engineers see you as someone who can actually unblock them, not just track their tickets. If you want to be the reason talented, overextended teams finally have the time and space to do their best work, this is that job.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What You'll Work On</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is our first Technical Program Manager opening; we’re looking for someone to bring order and momentum to our product and engineering teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reduce friction and streamline workflows across engineering and product teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactively communicate and resolve risks or issues before they impact progress</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Empower engineering teams to focus on high-value technical work instead of operational overhead</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the successful integration of technologies that meet the needs of Government, Enterprise, and Consumer customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clarify priorities and ownership across functional and deployment teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Encourage a culture of open communication</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bring structure to teams that don't fully have it yet; building the systems, rather than just running the ones that already exist</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own Jira hygiene, sprint planning, and ticket triage for teams handling high volumes of inbound work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run standups and cross-functional syncs that keep engineering, product, and other stakeholders aligned</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Go deep on the technical details of the products you support, you'll need to talk to engineers daily and actually understand what they're building</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help engineers stay focused on hard technical problems by taking operational overhead off their plates</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What We Value</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Autonomy: A proven ability to learn continuously, work independently, and make decisions with minimal supervision.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partnership: Experience brainstorming and iterating alongside product managers and designers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pragmatism: The ability to move quickly while building for the long term. You take a thoughtful, practical approach to solving complex problems, considering tradeoffs and avoiding over-engineering.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adaptability: Comfort working in a constantly evolving environment with dynamic objectives and direct user iteration.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communication: The ability to work collaboratively with both technical and non-technical teammates, understanding how technical decisions impact the end user.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mission-Driven: A deep-seated belief in the importance of digital privacy and security. You understand that the code we ship has real-world consequences and are driven to build systems that protect and empower users.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Experience</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A background as a software engineer (or comparable hands-on technical experience) before moving into a program/product role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ability to go deep on how a product actually works, hold your own in daily conversations with engineers, and help unblock them</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience working within a startup</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong Jira proficiency and hands-on experience running sprint planning and agile processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of understanding technically complex systems, even if you've never written production code yourself (e.g., you can describe how an HTTP request works)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience triaging and prioritizing a high volume of inbound tickets, bugs, and feature requests</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills, you can translate between technical and non-technical stakeholders clearly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">(Bonus Points) Prior experience supporting consumer products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">(Bonus Points) Prior experience supporting government or defense products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">(Bonus Points) Prior experience in a startup environment</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Compensation</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role based in New York, NY is $170,000 - $190,000 depending on level, experience, and interview performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our benefits include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stipends for</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Family-forming needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gender-affirming care</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Culture &amp; Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How to apply</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Click the link below to apply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT CAPE\n\nCape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.\n\nInstead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected and have privacy.\n\nWe didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.\n\nToday, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM\n\nAt Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nCape has never had a Technical Program Manager, which means our engineering teams are moving fast on some of the hardest problems in telecom without the connective tissue to move even faster. Tickets go untracked, standups happen inconsistently, priorities blur across teams, and brilliant engineers spend more time untangling processes than solving problems. You'll be the first person to fix that.\n\nThis is a builder's role, there's no playbook to inherit. You will design the systems, rituals, and rhythms our teams need from scratch, and prove their value fast enough that other teams start asking for you. You'll need to earn trust by going deep enough on the technology that engineers see you as someone who can actually unblock them, not just track their tickets. If you want to be the reason talented, overextended teams finally have the time and space to do their best work, this is that job.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL WORK ON\n\n - This is our first Technical Program Manager opening; we’re looking for someone to bring order and momentum to our product and engineering teams\n\n - Reduce friction and streamline workflows across engineering and product teams\n\n - Proactively communicate and resolve risks or issues before they impact progress\n\n - Empower engineering teams to focus on high-value technical work instead of operational overhead\n\n - Support the successful integration of technologies that meet the needs of Government, Enterprise, and Consumer customers\n\n - Clarify priorities and ownership across functional and deployment teams\n\n - Encourage a culture of open communication\n\n - Bring structure to teams that don't fully have it yet; building the systems, rather than just running the ones that already exist\n\n - Own Jira hygiene, sprint planning, and ticket triage for teams handling high volumes of inbound work\n\n - Run standups and cross-functional syncs that keep engineering, product, and other stakeholders aligned\n\n - Go deep on the technical details of the products you support, you'll need to talk to engineers daily and actually understand what they're building\n\n - Help engineers stay focused on hard technical problems by taking operational overhead off their plates\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE VALUE\n\n - Autonomy: A proven ability to learn continuously, work independently, and make decisions with minimal supervision.\n\n - Partnership: Experience brainstorming and iterating alongside product managers and designers.\n\n - Pragmatism: The ability to move quickly while building for the long term. You take a thoughtful, practical approach to solving complex problems, considering tradeoffs and avoiding over-engineering.\n\n - Adaptability: Comfort working in a constantly evolving environment with dynamic objectives and direct user iteration.\n\n - Communication: The ability to work collaboratively with both technical and non-technical teammates, understanding how technical decisions impact the end user.\n\n - Mission-Driven: A deep-seated belief in the importance of digital privacy and security. You understand that the code we ship has real-world consequences and are driven to build systems that protect and empower users.\n\n\n\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n - A background as a software engineer (or comparable hands-on technical experience) before moving into a program/product role\n\n - The ability to go deep on how a product actually works, hold your own in daily conversations with engineers, and help unblock them\n\n - Proven experience working within a startup\n\n - Strong Jira proficiency and hands-on experience running sprint planning and agile processes\n\n - A track record of understanding technically complex systems, even if you've never written production code yourself (e.g., you can describe how an HTTP request works)\n\n - Experience triaging and prioritizing a high volume of inbound tickets, bugs, and feature requests\n\n - Excellent communication skills, you can translate between technical and non-technical stakeholders clearly\n\n - (Bonus Points) Prior experience supporting consumer products\n\n - (Bonus Points) Prior experience supporting government or defense products\n\n - (Bonus Points) Prior experience in a startup environment\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nWe offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role based in New York, NY is $170,000 - $190,000 depending on level, experience, and interview performance.\n\nOur benefits include:\n\n - 401(k) match\n\n - 100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents\n\n - 12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)\n\n - Stipends for\n\n - Family-forming needs\n\n - Gender-affirming care\n\n - Unlimited PTO\n\n\n\n\nOUR CULTURE & VALUES\n\n - We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.\n\n - We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.\n\n - We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.\n\n - We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nClick the link below to apply.\n\nWe reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.\n\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"cc18572e-fa2f-46cb-94e9-fcac492314f8","title":"Forward Deployed Engineer, East Asia","department":"Engineering","team":"FDE","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"East Asia","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-09T14:39:00.187+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/cc18572e-fa2f-46cb-94e9-fcac492314f8","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/cc18572e-fa2f-46cb-94e9-fcac492314f8/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Cape</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected <em>and</em> have privacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Role</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Forward Deployed Engineers (FDEs) are the technical operators who ensure Cape’s products actually work in the field for the customers who depend on them most. In a world of demo-ware and big promises, FDEs delivers tangible outcomes: they embed with federal customers, translate ambiguous mission needs into working software, and feed hard-won demand signal back into product and engineering.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a hands-on builder role at the seam between Business Development and Engineering. You will be the customer’s technical advocate inside Cape and Cape’s technical advocate inside the customer’s building. You will scope deployments, prototype integrations, troubleshoot live issues on production networks, and pull engineering priorities directly from operator pain. Where the product doesn’t yet do what the mission requires, you will build the bridge—and then push the durable fix into the roadmap.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">FDE is a small, high-trust team. We're building this together. You will not be handed a playbook, you'll help write it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Work On</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Customer Deployment &amp; Delivery</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the technical delivery of Cape’s products into federal/national security/enterprise customer environments—from first prototype through operational acceptance and sustainment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Embed with customer teams around the world to understand workflows, threat models, and constraints that don’t appear in any requirements document</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Configure, integrate, and tune Cape’s mobile core capabilities against the specific mission profile of each deployment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead customer exercises, pilots, and demonstrations; structure them to produce decision-quality evidence rather than theater</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide direct technical support during live operations and incidents; conduct root-cause analyses and drive preventive fixes back into the platform</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Prototyping &amp; Engineering </strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write production-grade code to build the glue, integrations, tooling, and one-off capabilities that unblock customer deployments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prototype new product features in the field, validate them against real mission use, and work with core engineering teams to expand on successful hypotheses</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make sound tradeoffs between bespoke customer work and reusable platform investment—default toward the platform when the pattern repeats</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bridge Between Customer, Product, and Engineering</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate customer mission requirements into clear, prioritized engineering asks; then work alongside the broader engineering team to build the features that address them; translate engineering constraints back into language program officers and operators can act on</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advocate internally for customer priorities with concrete evidence: deployment data, operator quotes, blocking issues, and the cost of inaction</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product and Engineering leadership to inform the roadmap—surfacing patterns across deployments that warrant platform investment versus one-off solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Business Development and Solutions Architects on captures, pilots, and follow-on opportunities; provide the technical credibility that converts pilots into programs of record</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Embed with the broader engineering team to design and ship customer-specific features</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Experience</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in a software engineering or forward deployed engineering role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Fluency in Mandarin Chinese (spoken and written)</strong></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Based in (or willing to relocate/travel to) the Asia-Pacific region.</strong></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated technical competency across multiple domains—a “Swiss army knife” profile who can credibly code, debug networking issues, reason about systems-level tradeoffs, and learn quickly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong ability to scope ambiguous problems, sequence delivery, and make sound prioritization calls without explicit instruction</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication; able to brief a flag officer, write a clear engineering ticket, and run a customer working session with equal fluency</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High ownership and resourcefulness—comfort with the parts of the job that aren’t glamorous, and a track record of doing whatever needs to be done to deliver</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to engage directly with customers to scope technical requirements and deliver against them end to end</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willingness to travel up to 50% to customer sites, military installations, and partner locations</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Preferred</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in mobile networks, telecom, networking infrastructure, or cybersecurity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">U.S. citizenship and eligibility for a U.S. Top Secret security clearance (active TS strongly preferred).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior military service, government civilian experience, or time in roles involving communications, signals, cyber, or intelligence</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in a hands-on technical role with significant customer facing responsibilities—for example, a former FDE in a high growth startup, a startup engineer who carried customer deployments, or a defense tech deployment engineer (Palantir, Anduril, Shield AI, etc.)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience as an early engineer or operator at a high-growth startup—comfort with the ambiguity, pace, and missing infrastructure that comes with sub-100-person companies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience teaching, mentoring, or onboarding technical teammates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of taking field-driven feature work into a core product roadmap</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Compensation</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in NYC/DC is $175k-$235k depending on experience and interview performance and location.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our benefits include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stipends for</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Family-forming needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gender-affirming care</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Relocation and moving assistance if needed</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Culture &amp; Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How to apply</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Click the link below to apply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT CAPE\n\nCape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.\n\nInstead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected and have privacy.\n\nWe didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.\n\nToday, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM\n\nAt Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nForward Deployed Engineers (FDEs) are the technical operators who ensure Cape’s products actually work in the field for the customers who depend on them most. In a world of demo-ware and big promises, FDEs delivers tangible outcomes: they embed with federal customers, translate ambiguous mission needs into working software, and feed hard-won demand signal back into product and engineering.\n\n\n\nThis is a hands-on builder role at the seam between Business Development and Engineering. You will be the customer’s technical advocate inside Cape and Cape’s technical advocate inside the customer’s building. You will scope deployments, prototype integrations, troubleshoot live issues on production networks, and pull engineering priorities directly from operator pain. Where the product doesn’t yet do what the mission requires, you will build the bridge—and then push the durable fix into the roadmap.\n\n\n\nFDE is a small, high-trust team. We're building this together. You will not be handed a playbook, you'll help write it.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL WORK ON\n\nCustomer Deployment & Delivery\n\n - Own the technical delivery of Cape’s products into federal/national security/enterprise customer environments—from first prototype through operational acceptance and sustainment\n\n - Embed with customer teams around the world to understand workflows, threat models, and constraints that don’t appear in any requirements document\n\n - Configure, integrate, and tune Cape’s mobile core capabilities against the specific mission profile of each deployment\n\n - Lead customer exercises, pilots, and demonstrations; structure them to produce decision-quality evidence rather than theater\n\n - Provide direct technical support during live operations and incidents; conduct root-cause analyses and drive preventive fixes back into the platform\n   \n   \n\nPrototyping & Engineering \n\n - Write production-grade code to build the glue, integrations, tooling, and one-off capabilities that unblock customer deployments\n\n - Prototype new product features in the field, validate them against real mission use, and work with core engineering teams to expand on successful hypotheses\n\n - Make sound tradeoffs between bespoke customer work and reusable platform investment—default toward the platform when the pattern repeats\n   \n   \n\nBridge Between Customer, Product, and Engineering\n\n - Translate customer mission requirements into clear, prioritized engineering asks; then work alongside the broader engineering team to build the features that address them; translate engineering constraints back into language program officers and operators can act on\n\n - Advocate internally for customer priorities with concrete evidence: deployment data, operator quotes, blocking issues, and the cost of inaction\n\n - Partner with Product and Engineering leadership to inform the roadmap—surfacing patterns across deployments that warrant platform investment versus one-off solutions\n\n - Partner with Business Development and Solutions Architects on captures, pilots, and follow-on opportunities; provide the technical credibility that converts pilots into programs of record\n\n - Embed with the broader engineering team to design and ship customer-specific features\n   \n   \n\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n - 2+ years of experience in a software engineering or forward deployed engineering role\n\n - Fluency in Mandarin Chinese (spoken and written)\n\n - Based in (or willing to relocate/travel to) the Asia-Pacific region.\n\n - Demonstrated technical competency across multiple domains—a “Swiss army knife” profile who can credibly code, debug networking issues, reason about systems-level tradeoffs, and learn quickly\n\n - Strong ability to scope ambiguous problems, sequence delivery, and make sound prioritization calls without explicit instruction\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication; able to brief a flag officer, write a clear engineering ticket, and run a customer working session with equal fluency\n\n - High ownership and resourcefulness—comfort with the parts of the job that aren’t glamorous, and a track record of doing whatever needs to be done to deliver\n\n - Demonstrated ability to engage directly with customers to scope technical requirements and deliver against them end to end\n\n - Willingness to travel up to 50% to customer sites, military installations, and partner locations\n\n\n\n\nPREFERRED\n\n - Background in mobile networks, telecom, networking infrastructure, or cybersecurity\n\n - U.S. citizenship and eligibility for a U.S. Top Secret security clearance (active TS strongly preferred).\n\n - Prior military service, government civilian experience, or time in roles involving communications, signals, cyber, or intelligence\n\n - Experience in a hands-on technical role with significant customer facing responsibilities—for example, a former FDE in a high growth startup, a startup engineer who carried customer deployments, or a defense tech deployment engineer (Palantir, Anduril, Shield AI, etc.)\n\n - Experience as an early engineer or operator at a high-growth startup—comfort with the ambiguity, pace, and missing infrastructure that comes with sub-100-person companies\n\n - Experience teaching, mentoring, or onboarding technical teammates\n\n - Track record of taking field-driven feature work into a core product roadmap\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nWe offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in NYC/DC is $175k-$235k depending on experience and interview performance and location.\n\n\n\nOur benefits include:\n\n - 401(k) match\n\n - 100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents\n\n - 12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)\n\n - Stipends for\n   \n   - Family-forming needs\n   \n   - Gender-affirming care\n\n - Unlimited PTO\n\n - Relocation and moving assistance if needed\n\n\n\n\nOUR CULTURE & VALUES\n\n - We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.\n\n - We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.\n\n - We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.\n\n - We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nClick the link below to apply.\n\nWe reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.\n\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"8ea483bd-4753-45e3-933f-075412844a02","title":"Forward Deployed Engineer, Federal","department":"Engineering","team":"FDE","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Arlington, VA","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-09T14:54:22.992+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Virginia","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Arlington"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/8ea483bd-4753-45e3-933f-075412844a02","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/8ea483bd-4753-45e3-933f-075412844a02/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Cape</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected <em>and</em> have privacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Role</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Forward Deployed Engineers (FDEs) are the technical operators who ensure Cape’s products actually work in the field for the customers who depend on them most. In a world of demo-ware and big promises, FDEs delivers tangible outcomes: they embed with federal customers, translate ambiguous mission needs into working software, and feed hard-won demand signal back into product and engineering.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a hands-on builder role at the seam between Business Development and Engineering. You will be the customer’s technical advocate inside Cape and Cape’s technical advocate inside the customer’s building. You will scope deployments, prototype integrations, troubleshoot live issues on production networks, and pull engineering priorities directly from operator pain. Where the product doesn’t yet do what the mission requires, you will build the bridge—and then push the durable fix into the roadmap.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">FDE is a small, high-trust team. We're building this together. You will not be handed a playbook, you'll help write it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Work On</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer Deployment &amp; Delivery</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the technical delivery of Cape’s products into federal and national security customer environments—from first prototype through operational acceptance and sustainment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Embed with customer teams around the world to understand workflows, threat models, and constraints that don’t appear in any requirements document</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Configure, integrate, and tune Cape’s mobile core capabilities against the specific mission profile of each deployment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead customer exercises, pilots, and demonstrations; structure them to produce decision-quality evidence rather than theater</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide direct technical support during live operations and incidents; conduct root-cause analyses and drive preventive fixes back into the platform</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Prototyping &amp; Engineering</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write production-grade code to build the glue, integrations, tooling, and one-off capabilities that unblock customer deployments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prototype new product features in the field, validate them against real mission use, and work with core engineering teams to expand on successful hypotheses</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make sound tradeoffs between bespoke customer work and reusable platform investment—default toward the platform when the pattern repeats</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Bridge Between Customer, Product, and Engineering</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate customer mission requirements into clear, prioritized engineering asks; translate engineering constraints back into language program officers and operators can act on</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advocate internally for customer priorities with concrete evidence: deployment data, operator quotes, blocking issues, and the cost of inaction</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product and Engineering leadership to inform the roadmap—surfacing patterns across deployments that warrant platform investment versus one-off solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Business Development and Solutions Architects on captures, pilots, and follow-on opportunities; provide the technical credibility that converts pilots into programs of record</p></li></ul><h1></h1><h1><strong>Experience</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Required</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in a software engineering or forward deployed engineering role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated technical competency across multiple domains—a “Swiss army knife” profile who can credibly code, debug networking issues, reason about systems-level tradeoffs, and learn quickly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong ability to scope ambiguous problems, sequence delivery, and make sound prioritization calls without explicit instruction</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication; able to brief a flag officer, write a clear engineering ticket, and run a customer working session with equal fluency</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High ownership and resourcefulness—comfort with the parts of the job that aren’t glamorous, and a track record of doing whatever needs to be done to deliver</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to engage directly with customers to scope technical requirements and deliver against them end to end</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">U.S. citizenship and eligibility for a U.S. Top Secret security clearance (active TS strongly preferred)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willingness to travel up to 50% to customer sites, military installations, and partner locations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Washington, DC or New York-based or willing to relocate</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Preferred</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Active TS/SCI clearance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior military service, government civilian experience, or time in roles involving communications, signals, cyber, or intelligence</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in a hands-on technical role with significant customer facing responsibilities—for example, a former FDE in a high growth startup, a startup engineer who carried customer deployments, or a defense tech deployment engineer (Palantir, Anduril, Shield AI, etc.)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in mobile networks, telecom, networking infrastructure, or cybersecurity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience as an early engineer or operator at a high-growth startup—comfort with the ambiguity, pace, and missing infrastructure that comes with sub-100-person companies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience teaching, mentoring, or onboarding technical teammates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of taking field-driven feature work into a core product roadmap</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Compensation</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in New York, NY or Arlington, VA is $175k-$235k depending on experience and interview performance and location.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our benefits include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stipends for</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Family-forming needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gender-affirming care</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Culture &amp; Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How to apply</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Click the link below to apply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT CAPE\n\nCape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.\n\nInstead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected and have privacy.\n\nWe didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.\n\nToday, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM\n\nAt Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nForward Deployed Engineers (FDEs) are the technical operators who ensure Cape’s products actually work in the field for the customers who depend on them most. In a world of demo-ware and big promises, FDEs delivers tangible outcomes: they embed with federal customers, translate ambiguous mission needs into working software, and feed hard-won demand signal back into product and engineering.\n\n\n\nThis is a hands-on builder role at the seam between Business Development and Engineering. You will be the customer’s technical advocate inside Cape and Cape’s technical advocate inside the customer’s building. You will scope deployments, prototype integrations, troubleshoot live issues on production networks, and pull engineering priorities directly from operator pain. Where the product doesn’t yet do what the mission requires, you will build the bridge—and then push the durable fix into the roadmap.\n\n\n\nFDE is a small, high-trust team. We're building this together. You will not be handed a playbook, you'll help write it.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL WORK ON\n\nCustomer Deployment & Delivery\n\n - Own the technical delivery of Cape’s products into federal and national security customer environments—from first prototype through operational acceptance and sustainment\n\n - Embed with customer teams around the world to understand workflows, threat models, and constraints that don’t appear in any requirements document\n\n - Configure, integrate, and tune Cape’s mobile core capabilities against the specific mission profile of each deployment\n\n - Lead customer exercises, pilots, and demonstrations; structure them to produce decision-quality evidence rather than theater\n\n - Provide direct technical support during live operations and incidents; conduct root-cause analyses and drive preventive fixes back into the platform\n\n\nPROTOTYPING & ENGINEERING\n\n - Write production-grade code to build the glue, integrations, tooling, and one-off capabilities that unblock customer deployments\n\n - Prototype new product features in the field, validate them against real mission use, and work with core engineering teams to expand on successful hypotheses\n\n - Make sound tradeoffs between bespoke customer work and reusable platform investment—default toward the platform when the pattern repeats\n\n\nBRIDGE BETWEEN CUSTOMER, PRODUCT, AND ENGINEERING\n\n - Translate customer mission requirements into clear, prioritized engineering asks; translate engineering constraints back into language program officers and operators can act on\n\n - Advocate internally for customer priorities with concrete evidence: deployment data, operator quotes, blocking issues, and the cost of inaction\n\n - Partner with Product and Engineering leadership to inform the roadmap—surfacing patterns across deployments that warrant platform investment versus one-off solutions\n\n - Partner with Business Development and Solutions Architects on captures, pilots, and follow-on opportunities; provide the technical credibility that converts pilots into programs of record\n\n\n\n\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\nRequired\n\n - 2+ years of experience in a software engineering or forward deployed engineering role\n\n - Demonstrated technical competency across multiple domains—a “Swiss army knife” profile who can credibly code, debug networking issues, reason about systems-level tradeoffs, and learn quickly\n\n - Strong ability to scope ambiguous problems, sequence delivery, and make sound prioritization calls without explicit instruction\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication; able to brief a flag officer, write a clear engineering ticket, and run a customer working session with equal fluency\n\n - High ownership and resourcefulness—comfort with the parts of the job that aren’t glamorous, and a track record of doing whatever needs to be done to deliver\n\n - Demonstrated ability to engage directly with customers to scope technical requirements and deliver against them end to end\n\n - U.S. citizenship and eligibility for a U.S. Top Secret security clearance (active TS strongly preferred)\n\n - Willingness to travel up to 50% to customer sites, military installations, and partner locations\n\n - Washington, DC or New York-based or willing to relocate\n\n\nPREFERRED\n\n - Active TS/SCI clearance\n\n - Prior military service, government civilian experience, or time in roles involving communications, signals, cyber, or intelligence\n\n - Experience in a hands-on technical role with significant customer facing responsibilities—for example, a former FDE in a high growth startup, a startup engineer who carried customer deployments, or a defense tech deployment engineer (Palantir, Anduril, Shield AI, etc.)\n\n - Background in mobile networks, telecom, networking infrastructure, or cybersecurity\n\n - Experience as an early engineer or operator at a high-growth startup—comfort with the ambiguity, pace, and missing infrastructure that comes with sub-100-person companies\n\n - Experience teaching, mentoring, or onboarding technical teammates\n\n - Track record of taking field-driven feature work into a core product roadmap\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nWe offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in New York, NY or Arlington, VA is $175k-$235k depending on experience and interview performance and location.\n\nOur benefits include:\n\n - 401(k) match\n\n - 100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents\n\n - 12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)\n\n - Stipends for\n   \n   - Family-forming needs\n   \n   - Gender-affirming care\n\n - Unlimited PTO\n\n\n\n\nOUR CULTURE & VALUES\n\n - We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.\n\n - We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.\n\n - We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.\n\n - We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nClick the link below to apply.\n\nWe reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.\n\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"13f3921d-ace0-40e4-9b82-e00630878197","title":"Software Engineer, Developer Experience","department":"Engineering","team":"SRE","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York, NY","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-18T16:06:17.101+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"450 Park Avenue South","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/13f3921d-ace0-40e4-9b82-e00630878197","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/13f3921d-ace0-40e4-9b82-e00630878197/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Cape</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected <em>and</em> have privacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>The Role</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape's engineering team is small by design and ambitious by nature. We build cryptographic primitives, 5G core network functions, zero-trust edge systems, and threat detection pipelines — problems that don't have StackOverflow answers. The people doing that work deserve an environment that gets out of their way.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Developer Experience Engineer, your job is to make Cape's engineers measurably faster, less frustrated, and more confident in what they ship. That means owning the internal platforms, tooling, and workflows that engineering depends on — from CI/CD pipelines and local development environments to AI-assisted development workflows, test infrastructure, and release processes. This is not a support role. It is a product role where the customer is the engineering organization, the product is the development loop, and quality is measured in time-to-merge, build reliability, AI-augmented velocity, and the number of times an engineer has to context-switch to deal with infrastructure instead of product.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will work across the full engineering organization — embedded closely with platform, product, and security teams — and report to engineering leadership. Your impact will be felt by every engineer at Cape.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What You'll Work On</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Developer Tooling and Environments:</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain the internal tooling, scripts, and SDKs that Cape engineers use daily — from project scaffolding and local dev setup to testing utilities and debugging aids</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the local development environment story: containerized setups, secrets management, service dependencies, and onboarding time for new engineers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate and introduce new tools thoughtfully — instrument adoption, gather feedback, and deprecate what isn't working</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write the documentation and runbooks that make complex infrastructure accessible to engineers who shouldn't need to become infrastructure experts to use it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and implement infrastructure that enables engineers to go from code to deployed artifact quickly and with high confidence, regardless of which product surface they're working on</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive reliability improvements that eliminate common failure modes: flaky tests, non-reproducible builds, slow pipelines, and environment drift between local and CI</p></li></ul><h2><strong>AI Tooling and AI-Assisted Development:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own Cape’s AI-assisted development strategy — evaluate, integrate, and configure AI coding tools (code completion, automated review, agentic coding assistants) so engineers get high-quality suggestions that respect our security and compliance requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build guardrails and context systems that make AI tools effective in Cape’s codebase — prompt engineering for internal tooling, retrieval-augmented generation over internal docs, and repository-aware configurations that keep AI suggestions relevant and safe</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Measure the productivity impact of AI tooling rigorously — track adoption, code acceptance rates, time savings, and quality metrics to separate hype from genuine acceleration</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay ahead of the rapidly evolving AI development tooling landscape and bring informed recommendations to engineering leadership on what to adopt, what to build internally, and what to avoid</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Engineering Culture and Standards:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify patterns of friction across the engineering organization through observation, surveys, and direct partnership with teams — then prioritize and eliminate them</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to engineering standards around testing, code review, and deployment practices that help Cape's engineers ship with speed and confidence</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set a high bar for the developer experience through your own work — write code that other engineers will be glad to depend on</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Experience</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of software engineering experience, with meaningful time spent on internal platforms, developer tooling, or infrastructure</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of identifying developer friction, building solutions, and measuring the improvement — not just shipping tooling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in at least one modern backend language — Go is strongly preferred; Python, TypeScript, or Rust also welcome</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience improving and optimizing CI/CD systems (GitHub Actions, Buildkite, Bazel, or similar) at engineering-team scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of containerization and orchestration: Docker, Kubernetes, or other containers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal communication skills — you can explain infrastructure tradeoffs to engineers who didn't ask for a lecture and write docs that actually get read</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building developer platforms in security-constrained environments (FedRAMP, DISA STIGs, or government compliance frameworks)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with software supply chain security: artifact signing (Sigstore, Cosign), SBOM generation, dependency auditing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience at a high-growth startup where the engineering team scaled rapidly and tooling had to keep pace</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in observability tooling: distributed tracing, metrics pipelines, and making complex systems legible to engineers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience integrating AI coding assistants (GitHub Copilot, Claude Code, Cursor, or similar) into engineering workflows, including prompt tuning, context management, and measuring productivity impact</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Active U.S. security clearance or eligibility and willingness to obtain one</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in New York, New York is $225,000-$275,000 depending on experience and interview performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our benefits include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stipends for</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Family-forming needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gender-affirming care</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Culture &amp; Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How to apply</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Click the link below to apply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT CAPE\n\nCape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.\n\nInstead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected and have privacy.\n\nWe didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.\n\nToday, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM\n\nAt Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nCape's engineering team is small by design and ambitious by nature. We build cryptographic primitives, 5G core network functions, zero-trust edge systems, and threat detection pipelines — problems that don't have StackOverflow answers. The people doing that work deserve an environment that gets out of their way.\n\nAs a Developer Experience Engineer, your job is to make Cape's engineers measurably faster, less frustrated, and more confident in what they ship. That means owning the internal platforms, tooling, and workflows that engineering depends on — from CI/CD pipelines and local development environments to AI-assisted development workflows, test infrastructure, and release processes. This is not a support role. It is a product role where the customer is the engineering organization, the product is the development loop, and quality is measured in time-to-merge, build reliability, AI-augmented velocity, and the number of times an engineer has to context-switch to deal with infrastructure instead of product.\n\nYou will work across the full engineering organization — embedded closely with platform, product, and security teams — and report to engineering leadership. Your impact will be felt by every engineer at Cape.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL WORK ON\n\n\n\n\nDEVELOPER TOOLING AND ENVIRONMENTS:\n\n - Build and maintain the internal tooling, scripts, and SDKs that Cape engineers use daily — from project scaffolding and local dev setup to testing utilities and debugging aids\n\n - Own the local development environment story: containerized setups, secrets management, service dependencies, and onboarding time for new engineers\n\n - Evaluate and introduce new tools thoughtfully — instrument adoption, gather feedback, and deprecate what isn't working\n\n - Write the documentation and runbooks that make complex infrastructure accessible to engineers who shouldn't need to become infrastructure experts to use it\n\n - Design and implement infrastructure that enables engineers to go from code to deployed artifact quickly and with high confidence, regardless of which product surface they're working on\n\n - Drive reliability improvements that eliminate common failure modes: flaky tests, non-reproducible builds, slow pipelines, and environment drift between local and CI\n\n\nAI TOOLING AND AI-ASSISTED DEVELOPMENT:\n\n - Own Cape’s AI-assisted development strategy — evaluate, integrate, and configure AI coding tools (code completion, automated review, agentic coding assistants) so engineers get high-quality suggestions that respect our security and compliance requirements\n\n - Build guardrails and context systems that make AI tools effective in Cape’s codebase — prompt engineering for internal tooling, retrieval-augmented generation over internal docs, and repository-aware configurations that keep AI suggestions relevant and safe\n\n - Measure the productivity impact of AI tooling rigorously — track adoption, code acceptance rates, time savings, and quality metrics to separate hype from genuine acceleration\n\n - Stay ahead of the rapidly evolving AI development tooling landscape and bring informed recommendations to engineering leadership on what to adopt, what to build internally, and what to avoid\n\n\nENGINEERING CULTURE AND STANDARDS:\n\n - Identify patterns of friction across the engineering organization through observation, surveys, and direct partnership with teams — then prioritize and eliminate them\n\n - Contribute to engineering standards around testing, code review, and deployment practices that help Cape's engineers ship with speed and confidence\n\n - Set a high bar for the developer experience through your own work — write code that other engineers will be glad to depend on\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n - 4+ years of software engineering experience, with meaningful time spent on internal platforms, developer tooling, or infrastructure\n\n - A track record of identifying developer friction, building solutions, and measuring the improvement — not just shipping tooling\n\n - Fluency in at least one modern backend language — Go is strongly preferred; Python, TypeScript, or Rust also welcome\n\n - Hands-on experience improving and optimizing CI/CD systems (GitHub Actions, Buildkite, Bazel, or similar) at engineering-team scale\n\n - Strong understanding of containerization and orchestration: Docker, Kubernetes, or other containers.\n\n - Strong written and verbal communication skills — you can explain infrastructure tradeoffs to engineers who didn't ask for a lecture and write docs that actually get read\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience building developer platforms in security-constrained environments (FedRAMP, DISA STIGs, or government compliance frameworks)\n\n - Familiarity with software supply chain security: artifact signing (Sigstore, Cosign), SBOM generation, dependency auditing\n\n - Experience at a high-growth startup where the engineering team scaled rapidly and tooling had to keep pace\n\n - Background in observability tooling: distributed tracing, metrics pipelines, and making complex systems legible to engineers\n\n - Experience integrating AI coding assistants (GitHub Copilot, Claude Code, Cursor, or similar) into engineering workflows, including prompt tuning, context management, and measuring productivity impact\n\n - Active U.S. security clearance or eligibility and willingness to obtain one\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nWe offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in New York, New York is $225,000-$275,000 depending on experience and interview performance.\n\nOur benefits include:\n\n - 401(k) match\n\n - 100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents\n\n - 12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)\n\n - Stipends for\n   \n   - Family-forming needs\n   \n   - Gender-affirming care\n\n - Unlimited PTO\n\n\n\n\nOUR CULTURE & VALUES\n\n - We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.\n\n - We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.\n\n - We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.\n\n - We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nClick the link below to apply.\n\nWe reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.\n\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"5bec54ea-a51a-41b9-8da9-b9f2ff5f90a2","title":"Business Recruiter","department":"Internal Ops","team":"People","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York, NY","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Washington DC","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Washington DC","addressCountry":"USA"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-07-08T21:32:24.689+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"450 Park Avenue South","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/5bec54ea-a51a-41b9-8da9-b9f2ff5f90a2","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/5bec54ea-a51a-41b9-8da9-b9f2ff5f90a2/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Cape</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected <em>and</em> have privacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>The Role</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are building the most user-friendly recruiting and HR machine in the world to propel Cape’s growth. The right candidate treats every open role as a massive opportunity cost for the company. They move fast to manage, prioritize, and close searches.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">They develop practical and creative ways to identify leading talent, creating a world-class experience for Capers and candidates. They use data to benchmark, surface challenges, and set a new bar for process and quality. In summary, the right candidate, along with the hiring managers, builds high-performing teams that embody Cape’s values and culture.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a fast-paced, passionate environment in explosive growth mode - we need you to find the best of the best who will continue to make Cape a great company. This role reports to our Head of Operations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><h1>What You'll Work On</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meet (or exceed) weekly, monthly, quarterly recruiting goals and hiring targets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with hiring teams to deeply understand hiring needs and requirements of the role and the ideal candidate, and develop unique full cycle hiring strategies and interview criteria for each role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop a close business relationship with hiring managers, interview teams and executives to influence scoping of roles and ensuring interview team alignment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build talent pipelines for multiple technical job requisitions at any given time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run searches and engage with passive candidates via Ashby, LinkedIn, Google Search Engine, and other platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Execute and build effective sourcing, assessment, and closing approaches with an ability to manage hiring manager expectations through a deep understanding of return on investment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide positive and exceptional interview experiences for all parties</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Experience</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Relentless passion and drive to find and connect with the best talent</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years recruiting experience with an in-house recruiting team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in tech startups and demonstrated ability to achieve goals in a low structure, fast-paced environment in a flexible manner</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A sincere understanding of the importance of building relationships with active and passive candidates of all levels</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience in building and managing a diverse pipeline</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional organizational skills, with attention to detail and great follow-through</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passionate, driven mentality with the readiness to jump right in and go!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Keep ‘em warm! Manage the existing pipeline of candidates and identify potential opportunities for the future</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Compensation</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive compensation that is <strong>geo-adjusted</strong> based on <strong>your location</strong>, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in New York, New York and Arlington, VA is $150,000-$180,000 depending on experience and interview performance. Our benefits include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stipends for</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Family-forming needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gender-affirming care</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Culture &amp; Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How to apply</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Click the link below to apply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT CAPE\n\nCape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.\n\nInstead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected and have privacy.\n\nWe didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.\n\nToday, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM\n\nAt Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nWe are building the most user-friendly recruiting and HR machine in the world to propel Cape’s growth. The right candidate treats every open role as a massive opportunity cost for the company. They move fast to manage, prioritize, and close searches.\n\nThey develop practical and creative ways to identify leading talent, creating a world-class experience for Capers and candidates. They use data to benchmark, surface challenges, and set a new bar for process and quality. In summary, the right candidate, along with the hiring managers, builds high-performing teams that embody Cape’s values and culture.\n\nThis is a fast-paced, passionate environment in explosive growth mode - we need you to find the best of the best who will continue to make Cape a great company. This role reports to our Head of Operations.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL WORK ON\n\n - Meet (or exceed) weekly, monthly, quarterly recruiting goals and hiring targets\n\n - Partner with hiring teams to deeply understand hiring needs and requirements of the role and the ideal candidate, and develop unique full cycle hiring strategies and interview criteria for each role\n\n - Develop a close business relationship with hiring managers, interview teams and executives to influence scoping of roles and ensuring interview team alignment\n\n - Build talent pipelines for multiple technical job requisitions at any given time\n\n - Run searches and engage with passive candidates via Ashby, LinkedIn, Google Search Engine, and other platforms\n\n - Execute and build effective sourcing, assessment, and closing approaches with an ability to manage hiring manager expectations through a deep understanding of return on investment\n\n - Provide positive and exceptional interview experiences for all parties\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n - Relentless passion and drive to find and connect with the best talent\n\n - 4+ years recruiting experience with an in-house recruiting team\n\n - Experience in tech startups and demonstrated ability to achieve goals in a low structure, fast-paced environment in a flexible manner\n\n - A sincere understanding of the importance of building relationships with active and passive candidates of all levels\n\n - Proven experience in building and managing a diverse pipeline\n\n - Exceptional organizational skills, with attention to detail and great follow-through\n\n - Passionate, driven mentality with the readiness to jump right in and go!\n\n - Keep ‘em warm! Manage the existing pipeline of candidates and identify potential opportunities for the future\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nWe offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in New York, New York and Arlington, VA is $150,000-$180,000 depending on experience and interview performance. Our benefits include:\n\n - 401(k) match\n\n - 100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents\n\n - 12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)\n\n - Stipends for\n   \n   - Family-forming needs\n   \n   - Gender-affirming care\n\n - Unlimited PTO\n\n\n\n\nOUR CULTURE & VALUES\n\n - We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.\n\n - We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.\n\n - We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.\n\n - We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nClick the link below to apply.\n\nWe reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.\n\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"4d420e3e-8135-4866-9ba1-1ccd6c6be185","title":"Legal Counsel","department":"Internal Ops","team":"Internal Ops","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Arlington, VA","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-01T17:42:22.442+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Virginia","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Arlington"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/4d420e3e-8135-4866-9ba1-1ccd6c6be185","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/4d420e3e-8135-4866-9ba1-1ccd6c6be185/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Cape</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected <em>and</em> have privacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Role</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As our first in-house lawyer, this role is for someone who thrives at the intersection of law and model development - a builder with sharp instincts who is steady under ambiguity. You want to practice across a wide range of substantive areas, with real stakes, and with the latitude to make judgment calls.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll work directly across our business lines, including federal, enterprise, and consumer, navigating regulated spaces, government contracts, IP, commercial contracts, AI, employment, and everything in between. You'll manage a lean but high-quality roster of outside counsel, direct strategy and execute, and provide actionable guidance to our internal teams. If your version of a great legal career means breadth, autonomy, and the chance to build something from scratch, this is it</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Purpose</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Legal Counsel will be a key member of Cape’s Internal Operations team, enabling Cape to move at maximum velocity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll be the first dedicated lawyer on our team, reporting directly to our Head of Operations (a JD holder) helping to establish a legal function that scales.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Work On</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own legal needs across the company, spanning interactions with regulatory agencies, government and commercial contracts, employment matters, and IP risks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish, scale, and manage Cape’s internal legal processes, templates (eg MSAs, NDAs), and compliance frameworks (eg FCC, state licensing).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A long-term interest in a broad, general practice - whether that means GC one day or just continuing to do interesting work across a wide range of areas.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>As Cape grows, the problems we solve will continue to evolve. We optimize around solving important problems, not rigid or purple squirrel job descriptions.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Experience</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">JD from an accredited law school and active bar membership in good standing. Typically requires 6-8+ years of legal experience, ideally including top-tier law firm training.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A genuine interest in applying your training to a dynamic startup environment. You need to be the kind of lawyer who gets up to speed fast and earns the trust of engineers, sales professionals, and outside specialists alike.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The instincts of a builder: you're comfortable being the first person to own something, and you'd rather figure it out than wait for a playbook. You are already leveraging AI tools to simplify and scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to government contracts is a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating with ambiguity and across functions - you're as effective in a room with engineers as you are with outside counsel.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation:</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive compensation that is <strong>geo-adjusted</strong> based on <strong>your location</strong>, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in Washington, DC is $210,000-$250,000 depending on experience and interview performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our benefits include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stipends for</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Family-forming needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gender-affirming care</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Culture &amp; Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How to apply</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Click the link below to apply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT CAPE\n\nCape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.\n\nInstead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected and have privacy.\n\nWe didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.\n\nToday, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM\n\nAt Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nAs our first in-house lawyer, this role is for someone who thrives at the intersection of law and model development - a builder with sharp instincts who is steady under ambiguity. You want to practice across a wide range of substantive areas, with real stakes, and with the latitude to make judgment calls.\n\nYou'll work directly across our business lines, including federal, enterprise, and consumer, navigating regulated spaces, government contracts, IP, commercial contracts, AI, employment, and everything in between. You'll manage a lean but high-quality roster of outside counsel, direct strategy and execute, and provide actionable guidance to our internal teams. If your version of a great legal career means breadth, autonomy, and the chance to build something from scratch, this is it\n\n\n\n\nPURPOSE\n\n - The Legal Counsel will be a key member of Cape’s Internal Operations team, enabling Cape to move at maximum velocity.\n\n - You'll be the first dedicated lawyer on our team, reporting directly to our Head of Operations (a JD holder) helping to establish a legal function that scales.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL WORK ON\n\n - Own legal needs across the company, spanning interactions with regulatory agencies, government and commercial contracts, employment matters, and IP risks.\n\n - Establish, scale, and manage Cape’s internal legal processes, templates (eg MSAs, NDAs), and compliance frameworks (eg FCC, state licensing).\n\n - A long-term interest in a broad, general practice - whether that means GC one day or just continuing to do interesting work across a wide range of areas.\n\nAs Cape grows, the problems we solve will continue to evolve. We optimize around solving important problems, not rigid or purple squirrel job descriptions.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n - JD from an accredited law school and active bar membership in good standing. Typically requires 6-8+ years of legal experience, ideally including top-tier law firm training.\n\n - A genuine interest in applying your training to a dynamic startup environment. You need to be the kind of lawyer who gets up to speed fast and earns the trust of engineers, sales professionals, and outside specialists alike.\n\n - The instincts of a builder: you're comfortable being the first person to own something, and you'd rather figure it out than wait for a playbook. You are already leveraging AI tools to simplify and scale.\n\n - Exposure to government contracts is a plus.\n\n - Comfort operating with ambiguity and across functions - you're as effective in a room with engineers as you are with outside counsel.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION:\n\nWe offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in Washington, DC is $210,000-$250,000 depending on experience and interview performance.\n\nOur benefits include:\n\n - 401(k) match\n\n - Unlimited PTO\n\n - 100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents\n\n - 12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)\n\n - Stipends for\n   \n   - Family-forming needs\n   \n   - Gender-affirming care\n\n\n\n\nOUR CULTURE & VALUES\n\n - We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.\n\n - We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.\n\n - We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.\n\n - We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nClick the link below to apply.\n\nWe reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.\n\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"1905c6d7-6d9e-472d-acf8-6678c954464a","title":"Head of Government Relations","department":"Business Development","team":"BD","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Arlington, VA","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-17T18:05:13.150+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Virginia","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Arlington"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/1905c6d7-6d9e-472d-acf8-6678c954464a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/1905c6d7-6d9e-472d-acf8-6678c954464a/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Cape</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected <em>and</em> have privacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Opportunity</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is seeking a dedicated Head of Government Relations to map and engage federal stakeholders and to forecast policy-based risks and opportunities. While Cape's federal business development team engages end-user organizations, the Head of Government Relations will navigate complex policymaking to unlock national level relationships and funding. This role will also be key in setting milestones, forecasting policy changes, and anticipating regulatory requirements that could affect the company and its customers. This position will select and directly manage external advising and lobbying parties, requiring the right candidate to be able to both navigate human terrain and to clearly organize the company's government strategy. The ideal candidate will have at least five years of experience in legislative affairs, federal budget alignment, government contracting, policy planning, or similar arenas. This role reports to Cape's Head of Federal and will have an outsized impact on the success and growth of the company.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Purpose</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are seeking a high-ownership Head of Government Relations to serve as a critical driver of Cape's growth. In this role, you will take full accountability for government engagement and policy-based results through your management of external stakeholders. In addition, you will develop and maintain organized tracking systems to ensure cross-functional alignment on key lines of effort. Your mission is to bridge the gap between the company's most pressing intragovernmental challenges and the government institutions that can solve them. You will optimize external engagement through clearly communicated long-term strategies, while remaining responsive to the fluid nature of technology and defense policy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What You'll Work On</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Developing a long-term milestone-based government strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mapping key government stakeholders to company needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Forecasting political, policy, budgetary, and regulatory changes and volatility</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Shaping new policies beneficial to the company and its customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Forming and maturing partnerships with third parties in the federal ecosystem</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Optimizing relationships with external advisors, experts, and lobbyists</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engaging resource sponsors to achieve established strategic endstates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establishing, attending, and managing events that cross between industry and government affairs</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Experience</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Operational Pedigree: Prior experience in fast-paced environments. We value a background of \"ownership\" where you’ve been responsible for end-to-end outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">External Relationship Development: Ability to network among a diverse set of external stakeholders, build connections with them, and maintain strong ties.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Executive Communication: Clear and concise professional correspondence and awareness of protocol in political and bureaucratic offices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of the Legislative Process: First hand knowledge of the federal legislative process through experience in lobbying, Congressional fellowship, PSM/MLA, or similar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic Planning: Ability to establish a multi-year government engagement plan that aligns company goals with government cadences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional Background: Relevant background in Political Science, Public Administration, Public Policy, or similar professions.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in Arlington, VA is $250,000-$350,000 depending on experience and interview performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our benefits include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stipends for</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Family-forming needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gender-affirming care</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Culture &amp; Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How to apply</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Click the link below to apply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT CAPE\n\nCape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.\n\nInstead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected and have privacy.\n\nWe didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.\n\nToday, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM\n\nAt Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.\n\n\n\n\nTHE OPPORTUNITY\n\nCape is seeking a dedicated Head of Government Relations to map and engage federal stakeholders and to forecast policy-based risks and opportunities. While Cape's federal business development team engages end-user organizations, the Head of Government Relations will navigate complex policymaking to unlock national level relationships and funding. This role will also be key in setting milestones, forecasting policy changes, and anticipating regulatory requirements that could affect the company and its customers. This position will select and directly manage external advising and lobbying parties, requiring the right candidate to be able to both navigate human terrain and to clearly organize the company's government strategy. The ideal candidate will have at least five years of experience in legislative affairs, federal budget alignment, government contracting, policy planning, or similar arenas. This role reports to Cape's Head of Federal and will have an outsized impact on the success and growth of the company.\n\n\n\n\nPURPOSE\n\nWe are seeking a high-ownership Head of Government Relations to serve as a critical driver of Cape's growth. In this role, you will take full accountability for government engagement and policy-based results through your management of external stakeholders. In addition, you will develop and maintain organized tracking systems to ensure cross-functional alignment on key lines of effort. Your mission is to bridge the gap between the company's most pressing intragovernmental challenges and the government institutions that can solve them. You will optimize external engagement through clearly communicated long-term strategies, while remaining responsive to the fluid nature of technology and defense policy.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL WORK ON\n\n - Developing a long-term milestone-based government strategy\n\n - Mapping key government stakeholders to company needs\n\n - Forecasting political, policy, budgetary, and regulatory changes and volatility\n\n - Shaping new policies beneficial to the company and its customers\n\n - Forming and maturing partnerships with third parties in the federal ecosystem\n\n - Optimizing relationships with external advisors, experts, and lobbyists\n\n - Engaging resource sponsors to achieve established strategic endstates\n\n - Establishing, attending, and managing events that cross between industry and government affairs\n\n\n\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n - Operational Pedigree: Prior experience in fast-paced environments. We value a background of \"ownership\" where you’ve been responsible for end-to-end outcomes.\n\n - External Relationship Development: Ability to network among a diverse set of external stakeholders, build connections with them, and maintain strong ties.\n\n - Executive Communication: Clear and concise professional correspondence and awareness of protocol in political and bureaucratic offices.\n\n - Knowledge of the Legislative Process: First hand knowledge of the federal legislative process through experience in lobbying, Congressional fellowship, PSM/MLA, or similar.\n\n - Strategic Planning: Ability to establish a multi-year government engagement plan that aligns company goals with government cadences.\n\n - Professional Background: Relevant background in Political Science, Public Administration, Public Policy, or similar professions.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nWe offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in Arlington, VA is $250,000-$350,000 depending on experience and interview performance.\n\nOur benefits include:\n\n - 401(k) match\n\n - 100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents\n\n - 12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)\n\n - Stipends for\n   \n   - Family-forming needs\n   \n   - Gender-affirming care\n\n - Unlimited PTO\n\n\n\n\nOUR CULTURE & VALUES\n\n - We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.\n\n - We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.\n\n - We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.\n\n - We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nClick the link below to apply.\n\nWe reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.\n\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"74b860e6-1e8f-4bda-9f97-9aede0b0253f","title":"IT Support Specialist","department":"Internal Ops","team":"IT & Facilities","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York, NY","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-03T18:06:54.760+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"450 Park Avenue South","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/74b860e6-1e8f-4bda-9f97-9aede0b0253f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/74b860e6-1e8f-4bda-9f97-9aede0b0253f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Cape</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected <em>and</em> have privacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Role</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for an Onsite IT Support Specialist to be the friendly, first line of IT support for our NY office. You'll own the day-to-day employee IT experience from a great day-one onboarding, to fast resolution of everyday support requests, to a smooth offboarding. You will also keep our hardware inventory accurate and our onsite spaces (desks, conference rooms, AV) ready to go.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Work on</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Be the face of IT in our NY office</strong>. You’ll be the go-to for hands-on help today, and a key voice in designing the IT buildout of new spaces.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own IT onboarding through hypergrowth.</strong> You'll run a smooth day-one experience at a pace of multiple starts bi-weekly and make the process measurably better every cycle: automate provisioning, cut setup time, and raise the bar for what a first day feels like.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own Tier-1 resolution against SLA, then beat it.</strong> You'll work alongside our internal AI agent and build the automations and AI workflows that drive down resolve time and drive up customer satisfaction. Efficiency here isn't a buzzword; it's your scoreboard.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build our asset-management system from the ground up</strong>. You’ll own laptops, peripherals, and specialty hardware across two offices, international travelers, and remote employees — and make it audit-ready as we take on certifications like CMMC Level 2.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shape Cape's physical IT presence.</strong> You’ll be at the forefront of new offices, conference-room and AV tech, visitor systems with a mandate to bring in the best technology out there, not just keep the lights on.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Live in ambiguity and learn fast.</strong> Our integration surface grows monthly — new vendor and tools arrive weekly, each needing evaluation, SSO/SCIM, device packaging, and documentation. Learning has never been easier; you'll be expected to use every tool available and ship.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What We Value</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make technology invisible. Every Cape employee — from their first hour on day one — should be able to do their best work on our privacy and national security mission without IT ever being the thing that slows them down.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Turn hypergrowth into a smooth ride. Rapid hiring, new offices, and new tools arriving weekly could easily become chaos; this role exists to make scale feel effortless for the people living through it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Keep us fast and accountable. Speed can't come at the cost of trust — every device, access grant, and piece of hardware stays tracked, secure, and audit-ready as we grow into certifications like CMMC and SOC 2.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Experience</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2-3+ years of experience in IT support, particularly in a dynamic and evolving tech environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience supporting Apple/macOS laptops (and comfort across Windows and linux where needed).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with mobile device management (Iru, Jamf, or similar).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in a ticketing/helpdesk system (e.g., Jira Service Management) and working to SLAs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability in setting up, troubleshooting, and maintaining conference room hardware and software.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort with Google Workspace and/or Microsoft 365 administration basics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of effectively managing IT hardware procurement and inventory.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong problem-solving skills and ability to provide timely resolution to hardware and software issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong customer-service instincts, clear communication, and reliable follow-through.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Eagerness to work on projects that have a real-world impact on privacy and national security.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">May require lifting or carrying desktop computers up to 25 lbs<br /></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive compensation that is <strong>geo-adjusted</strong> based on <strong>your location</strong>, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in New York, NY is $85,000-$105,000 depending on experience and interview performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our benefits include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stipends for</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Family-forming needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gender-affirming care</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Culture &amp; Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How to apply</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Click the link below to apply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT CAPE\n\nCape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.\n\nInstead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected and have privacy.\n\nWe didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.\n\nToday, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM\n\nAt Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nWe're looking for an Onsite IT Support Specialist to be the friendly, first line of IT support for our NY office. You'll own the day-to-day employee IT experience from a great day-one onboarding, to fast resolution of everyday support requests, to a smooth offboarding. You will also keep our hardware inventory accurate and our onsite spaces (desks, conference rooms, AV) ready to go.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL WORK ON\n\n - Be the face of IT in our NY office. You’ll be the go-to for hands-on help today, and a key voice in designing the IT buildout of new spaces.\n\n - Own IT onboarding through hypergrowth. You'll run a smooth day-one experience at a pace of multiple starts bi-weekly and make the process measurably better every cycle: automate provisioning, cut setup time, and raise the bar for what a first day feels like.\n\n - Own Tier-1 resolution against SLA, then beat it. You'll work alongside our internal AI agent and build the automations and AI workflows that drive down resolve time and drive up customer satisfaction. Efficiency here isn't a buzzword; it's your scoreboard.\n\n - Build our asset-management system from the ground up. You’ll own laptops, peripherals, and specialty hardware across two offices, international travelers, and remote employees — and make it audit-ready as we take on certifications like CMMC Level 2.\n\n - Shape Cape's physical IT presence. You’ll be at the forefront of new offices, conference-room and AV tech, visitor systems with a mandate to bring in the best technology out there, not just keep the lights on.\n\n - Live in ambiguity and learn fast. Our integration surface grows monthly — new vendor and tools arrive weekly, each needing evaluation, SSO/SCIM, device packaging, and documentation. Learning has never been easier; you'll be expected to use every tool available and ship.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE VALUE\n\n - Make technology invisible. Every Cape employee — from their first hour on day one — should be able to do their best work on our privacy and national security mission without IT ever being the thing that slows them down.\n\n - Turn hypergrowth into a smooth ride. Rapid hiring, new offices, and new tools arriving weekly could easily become chaos; this role exists to make scale feel effortless for the people living through it.\n\n - Keep us fast and accountable. Speed can't come at the cost of trust — every device, access grant, and piece of hardware stays tracked, secure, and audit-ready as we grow into certifications like CMMC and SOC 2.\n\n\n\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n - 2-3+ years of experience in IT support, particularly in a dynamic and evolving tech environment.\n\n - Hands-on experience supporting Apple/macOS laptops (and comfort across Windows and linux where needed).\n\n - Familiarity with mobile device management (Iru, Jamf, or similar).\n\n - Experience working in a ticketing/helpdesk system (e.g., Jira Service Management) and working to SLAs.\n\n - Demonstrated ability in setting up, troubleshooting, and maintaining conference room hardware and software.\n\n - Comfort with Google Workspace and/or Microsoft 365 administration basics.\n\n - Proven track record of effectively managing IT hardware procurement and inventory.\n\n - Strong problem-solving skills and ability to provide timely resolution to hardware and software issues.\n\n - Strong customer-service instincts, clear communication, and reliable follow-through.\n\n - Eagerness to work on projects that have a real-world impact on privacy and national security.\n\n - May require lifting or carrying desktop computers up to 25 lbs\n   \n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nWe offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in New York, NY is $85,000-$105,000 depending on experience and interview performance.\n\nOur benefits include:\n\n - 401(k) match\n\n - Unlimited PTO\n\n - 100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents\n\n - 12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)\n\n - Stipends for\n   \n   - Family-forming needs\n   \n   - Gender-affirming care\n\n\n\n\nOUR CULTURE & VALUES\n\n - We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.\n\n - We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.\n\n - We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.\n\n - We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nClick the link below to apply.\n\nWe reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.\n\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"6bd192fd-6a04-464b-8c57-91f8949aa860","title":"Revenue Operations Manager","department":"Internal Ops","team":"Internal Ops","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York, NY","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-21T18:01:54.885+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"450 Park Avenue South","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/6bd192fd-6a04-464b-8c57-91f8949aa860","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/6bd192fd-6a04-464b-8c57-91f8949aa860/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Cape</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected <em>and</em> have privacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Role</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a Revenue Operations Manager to own and scale the systems, processes, and analytics that power our go-to-market engine. You'll sit at the intersection of Business Development, Operations, and Finance - turning messy processes into clean, automated, data-driven workflows, and giving leadership the visibility they need to make good decisions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a hands-on role for someone who's equally comfortable architecting a Salesforce data model, running a forecast cadence, and investing in enablement to scale our BD org. You'll partner closely with sales leadership and cross-functional stakeholders to remove friction across the revenue lifecycle - from lead to renewal.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Work On</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Systems &amp; Data</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the CRM (Salesforce) data layer: Object model, field definitions, pipeline data integrity, and the hygiene processes that keep the data trustworthy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate, select, and integrate GTM tools, making thoughtful build-vs-buy decisions as the tech stack scales.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with data/analytics teams to ensure CRM data flows cleanly into downstream reporting and BI systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain reporting and dashboards that give sales and executive leadership visibility into pipeline health, conversion, and rep performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support monthly/quarterly business reviews with clear, data-backed narratives.</p></li></ul></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Process &amp; Deal Support</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own or support deal desk operations: Approval workflows, non-standard deal structuring, and SLA management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document and continuously improve sales processes and methodology to ensure consistent execution from prospecting through close.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Ops to ensure seamless implementations, as well as create automations to help the team proactively manage the customer lifecycle.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enable on-target fulfillment from Ops to the customer through detailed information management and clear communication.</p></li></ul></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Cross-Functional Partnership</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as the operational thought partner to Business Development, Operations, and Finance leadership, translating business needs into scalable systems and processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure BD is enabled, training the team on the most up to date pricing strategy, proactively creating customer facing collateral, or educating the team on the latest product SKUs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate clearly with both technical and non-technical stakeholders, including executive audiences.</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Experience</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of experience in Revenue Operations, Sales Operations, GTM Systems, or a closely related role, ideally in B2B SaaS or defense tech.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong hands-on experience with Salesforce (administration, reporting, data model design); certification a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid analytical skills - comfortable working in SQL, Excel/Sheets, and BI tools (e.g., Looker, Tableau, Power BI).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience owning or heavily supporting a forecasting cadence and pipeline reporting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with the broader revenue tech stack (marketing automation, sales engagement, CPQ, BI, and data warehouse tools).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of turning ambiguous, messy problems into documented, scalable processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to work cross-functionally and present to leadership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A builder's mindset: bias toward action, comfortable prototyping a solution rather than waiting for a perfect spec.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>COMPENSATION:</strong> $150k - $180k</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Culture &amp; Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How to apply</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Click the link below to apply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT CAPE\n\nCape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.\n\nInstead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected and have privacy.\n\nWe didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.\n\nToday, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM\n\nAt Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nWe're looking for a Revenue Operations Manager to own and scale the systems, processes, and analytics that power our go-to-market engine. You'll sit at the intersection of Business Development, Operations, and Finance - turning messy processes into clean, automated, data-driven workflows, and giving leadership the visibility they need to make good decisions.\n\n\n\nThis is a hands-on role for someone who's equally comfortable architecting a Salesforce data model, running a forecast cadence, and investing in enablement to scale our BD org. You'll partner closely with sales leadership and cross-functional stakeholders to remove friction across the revenue lifecycle - from lead to renewal.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL WORK ON\n\n - Systems & Data\n   \n   - Own the CRM (Salesforce) data layer: Object model, field definitions, pipeline data integrity, and the hygiene processes that keep the data trustworthy.\n   \n   - Evaluate, select, and integrate GTM tools, making thoughtful build-vs-buy decisions as the tech stack scales.\n   \n   - Partner with data/analytics teams to ensure CRM data flows cleanly into downstream reporting and BI systems.\n   \n   - Build and maintain reporting and dashboards that give sales and executive leadership visibility into pipeline health, conversion, and rep performance.\n   \n   - Support monthly/quarterly business reviews with clear, data-backed narratives.\n\n - Process & Deal Support\n   \n   - Own or support deal desk operations: Approval workflows, non-standard deal structuring, and SLA management.\n   \n   - Document and continuously improve sales processes and methodology to ensure consistent execution from prospecting through close.\n   \n   - Partner with Ops to ensure seamless implementations, as well as create automations to help the team proactively manage the customer lifecycle.\n   \n   - Enable on-target fulfillment from Ops to the customer through detailed information management and clear communication.\n\n - Cross-Functional Partnership\n   \n   - Act as the operational thought partner to Business Development, Operations, and Finance leadership, translating business needs into scalable systems and processes.\n   \n   - Ensure BD is enabled, training the team on the most up to date pricing strategy, proactively creating customer facing collateral, or educating the team on the latest product SKUs.\n   \n   - Communicate clearly with both technical and non-technical stakeholders, including executive audiences.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n - 4+ years of experience in Revenue Operations, Sales Operations, GTM Systems, or a closely related role, ideally in B2B SaaS or defense tech.\n\n - Strong hands-on experience with Salesforce (administration, reporting, data model design); certification a plus.\n\n - Solid analytical skills - comfortable working in SQL, Excel/Sheets, and BI tools (e.g., Looker, Tableau, Power BI).\n\n - Experience owning or heavily supporting a forecasting cadence and pipeline reporting.\n\n - Familiarity with the broader revenue tech stack (marketing automation, sales engagement, CPQ, BI, and data warehouse tools).\n\n - A track record of turning ambiguous, messy problems into documented, scalable processes.\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to work cross-functionally and present to leadership.\n\n - A builder's mindset: bias toward action, comfortable prototyping a solution rather than waiting for a perfect spec.\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION: $150k - $180k\n\n\n\n\nOUR CULTURE & VALUES\n\n - We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.\n\n - We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.\n\n - We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.\n\n - We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nClick the link below to apply.\n\nWe reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.\n\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"62701150-1822-4ed4-96a4-0ffa89055428","title":"Capture Manager","department":"Internal Ops","team":"Internal Ops","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Arlington, VA","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-28T21:08:45.815+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Virginia","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Arlington"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/62701150-1822-4ed4-96a4-0ffa89055428","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/62701150-1822-4ed4-96a4-0ffa89055428/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Cape</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected <em>and</em> have privacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>The Role</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a Capture Manager to help drive new business growth with government and defense customers. This role sits at the center of our growth engine - owning opportunities from early market research and capture planning through proposal development and contract award.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll work closely with business development, engineering, program management, finance, and executive leadership to identify opportunities, build winning capture strategies, and produce compelling technical and pricing narratives that convert pursuits into awarded contracts. This is a hands-on role for someone who thrives in a fast-paced environment, is comfortable owning a process end-to-end, and can translate complex technical capabilities into clear, persuasive customer-facing content.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><h1>What You'll Work On</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Market &amp; Capture Strategy: </strong>Conduct ongoing market research to identify new business opportunities, using open-source tools (e.g., <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://SAM.gov\">SAM.gov</a>) and/or subscription intelligence services. Monitor emerging programs, solicitations, and customer priorities relevant to your assigned portfolio. Perform competitive analysis to inform opportunity qualification, teaming decisions, and win-theme development. Qualify opportunities and assess probability of win in partnership with capture and BD leadership. Build capture plans - both strategic (pipeline-level) and tactical (opportunity-specific) - aligned to growth targets.Develop win themes and strategic messaging for customer engagements and proposals. Represent the company at industry days, conferences, and customer meetings.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Proposal &amp; Content Development: </strong>Own and write responses to government and commercial RFIs, RFQs, RFPs, and white papers - ranging from short capability statements to large, multi-volume technical proposals. Coordinate with technical subject matter experts to accurately translate engineering capabilities into clear, compelling proposal narratives. Provide proposal strategy recommendations based on solicitation requirements and customer preferences. Build and maintain a reusable content library (boilerplate, graphics, past-performance write-ups) to improve proposal speed and quality over time. Own the proposal development process end-to-end, with a focus on continuous improvement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Pricing &amp; Deal Support: </strong>Support development and implementation of pricing strategy for your assigned portfolio or customer set. Coordinate cross-functional inputs (finance, contracts, program management) to ensure pricing and terms are accurate and competitive.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Cross-Functional Collaboration: </strong>Serve as a connective link between growth/BD, engineering, program management, legal, finance, and executive stakeholders to keep pursuits coordinated and on schedule. Translate customer priorities and feedback into internal roadmap and engineering input where relevant. Flag new opportunities to internal stakeholders as they're identified.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Experience</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3-5 years of experience in business development, capture management, proposal writing, or a related role supporting government or defense contracting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Current active US Secret clearance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of government procurement processes and the full capture/proposal lifecycle (market research through award).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills - able to turn complex technical or programmatic information into clear, persuasive content under tight deadlines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working across a wide range of stakeholders (engineering, program management, finance, legal, security) in a fast-paced, deadline-driven environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational skills and ability to manage multiple concurrent pursuits with overlapping timelines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-starter who can find information and make progress without extensive guidance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willingness to travel for customer meetings and industry events.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree or equivalent practical experience.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in Arlington, VA is $150,000-$180,000 depending on experience and interview performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our benefits include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stipends for</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Family-forming needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gender-affirming care</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Culture &amp; Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How to apply</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Click the link below to apply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT CAPE\n\nCape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.\n\nInstead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected and have privacy.\n\nWe didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.\n\nToday, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM\n\nAt Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nWe're looking for a Capture Manager to help drive new business growth with government and defense customers. This role sits at the center of our growth engine - owning opportunities from early market research and capture planning through proposal development and contract award.\n\nYou'll work closely with business development, engineering, program management, finance, and executive leadership to identify opportunities, build winning capture strategies, and produce compelling technical and pricing narratives that convert pursuits into awarded contracts. This is a hands-on role for someone who thrives in a fast-paced environment, is comfortable owning a process end-to-end, and can translate complex technical capabilities into clear, persuasive customer-facing content.\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL WORK ON\n\n - Market & Capture Strategy: Conduct ongoing market research to identify new business opportunities, using open-source tools (e.g., SAM.gov http://SAM.gov) and/or subscription intelligence services. Monitor emerging programs, solicitations, and customer priorities relevant to your assigned portfolio. Perform competitive analysis to inform opportunity qualification, teaming decisions, and win-theme development. Qualify opportunities and assess probability of win in partnership with capture and BD leadership. Build capture plans - both strategic (pipeline-level) and tactical (opportunity-specific) - aligned to growth targets.Develop win themes and strategic messaging for customer engagements and proposals. Represent the company at industry days, conferences, and customer meetings.\n\n - Proposal & Content Development: Own and write responses to government and commercial RFIs, RFQs, RFPs, and white papers - ranging from short capability statements to large, multi-volume technical proposals. Coordinate with technical subject matter experts to accurately translate engineering capabilities into clear, compelling proposal narratives. Provide proposal strategy recommendations based on solicitation requirements and customer preferences. Build and maintain a reusable content library (boilerplate, graphics, past-performance write-ups) to improve proposal speed and quality over time. Own the proposal development process end-to-end, with a focus on continuous improvement.\n\n - Pricing & Deal Support: Support development and implementation of pricing strategy for your assigned portfolio or customer set. Coordinate cross-functional inputs (finance, contracts, program management) to ensure pricing and terms are accurate and competitive.\n\n - Cross-Functional Collaboration: Serve as a connective link between growth/BD, engineering, program management, legal, finance, and executive stakeholders to keep pursuits coordinated and on schedule. Translate customer priorities and feedback into internal roadmap and engineering input where relevant. Flag new opportunities to internal stakeholders as they're identified.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n - 3-5 years of experience in business development, capture management, proposal writing, or a related role supporting government or defense contracting.\n\n - Current active US Secret clearance.\n\n - Strong understanding of government procurement processes and the full capture/proposal lifecycle (market research through award).\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills - able to turn complex technical or programmatic information into clear, persuasive content under tight deadlines.\n\n - Comfortable working across a wide range of stakeholders (engineering, program management, finance, legal, security) in a fast-paced, deadline-driven environment.\n\n - Strong organizational skills and ability to manage multiple concurrent pursuits with overlapping timelines.\n\n - Self-starter who can find information and make progress without extensive guidance.\n\n - Willingness to travel for customer meetings and industry events.\n\n - Bachelor's degree or equivalent practical experience.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nWe offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in Arlington, VA is $150,000-$180,000 depending on experience and interview performance.\n\nOur benefits include:\n\n - 401(k) match\n\n - 100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents\n\n - 12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)\n\n - Stipends for\n   \n   - Family-forming needs\n   \n   - Gender-affirming care\n\n - Unlimited PTO\n\n\n\n\nOUR CULTURE & VALUES\n\n - We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.\n\n - We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.\n\n - We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.\n\n - We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nClick the link below to apply.\n\nWe reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.\n\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"9649a783-82af-4e4e-9cc6-182bf201f8fc","title":"Business Intelligence and Research Manager","department":"Internal Ops","team":"Internal Ops","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York, NY","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-28T11:55:13.559+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"450 Park Avenue South","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/9649a783-82af-4e4e-9cc6-182bf201f8fc","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/9649a783-82af-4e4e-9cc6-182bf201f8fc/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Cape</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected <em>and</em> have privacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Role</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will be the analytical engine behind Cape's biggest consumer business decisions - pairing rigorous market research with sharp business intelligence to tell us what customers want, what they'll pay, and what it means for the bottom line. You'll design the studies that surface the \"why\" behind customer behavior and build the models that translate those insights into pricing, budgets, and margin plans leaders can act on. The ideal candidate is equally at home fielding a survey and building a P&amp;L, and can carry a finding all the way from raw data to a recommendation in front of the executive team. This role reports to our Head of Consumer Growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Work On</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><u>Metrics</u>: Define and develop business-unit metrics and associated dashboards that quantify the health of our business. This may require you to implement and optimize the internal systems to track those metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><u>Insights</u>: Dig into data, both quantitative and qualitative, to deliver strategic and actionable insights on topics like willingness-to-pay, feature trade-offs, and optimal plans structure and tiering. You’re as comfortable writing an SQL query as you are getting on a call with a customer to conduct a user interview.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><u>Planning</u>: You will build financial models and projections, appropriately benchmarked with well-founded and sourced assumptions, and track progress towards and deviation from goal. You can model the ROI of individual investment decisions, sizing the upside, framing the risk, and pressure-testing assumptions.<br /></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Experience</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of consulting, banking, investing, or business intelligence or market research experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical aptitude. You intuitively think about problems in terms of numbers and models, and you are able to quickly execute analyses in Excel or SQL. We will test you on this. You must feel comfortable with statistical tools and running methodologically sound surveys. Prior experience running brand surveys and creative testing is a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency with tools and using AI to work faster and smarter with data, and the judgement to know when the output is right and when it looks off.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to present findings and recommendations to a senior leadership audience, fielding challenges and incorporating feedback.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Structured and logical thinker with the ability to quickly get up to speed on new industries, products, and challenges.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-driven and relentlessly proactive. You don’t need someone to tell you to “move”. You just move. We’d rather have to tell you to slow down than to speed up.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comp: 150k - 185k</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Culture &amp; Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How to apply</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Click the link below to apply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT CAPE\n\nCape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.\n\nInstead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected and have privacy.\n\nWe didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.\n\nToday, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM\n\nAt Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nYou will be the analytical engine behind Cape's biggest consumer business decisions - pairing rigorous market research with sharp business intelligence to tell us what customers want, what they'll pay, and what it means for the bottom line. You'll design the studies that surface the \"why\" behind customer behavior and build the models that translate those insights into pricing, budgets, and margin plans leaders can act on. The ideal candidate is equally at home fielding a survey and building a P&L, and can carry a finding all the way from raw data to a recommendation in front of the executive team. This role reports to our Head of Consumer Growth.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL WORK ON\n\n - Metrics: Define and develop business-unit metrics and associated dashboards that quantify the health of our business. This may require you to implement and optimize the internal systems to track those metrics.\n\n - Insights: Dig into data, both quantitative and qualitative, to deliver strategic and actionable insights on topics like willingness-to-pay, feature trade-offs, and optimal plans structure and tiering. You’re as comfortable writing an SQL query as you are getting on a call with a customer to conduct a user interview.\n\n - Planning: You will build financial models and projections, appropriately benchmarked with well-founded and sourced assumptions, and track progress towards and deviation from goal. You can model the ROI of individual investment decisions, sizing the upside, framing the risk, and pressure-testing assumptions.\n   \n\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n - 4+ years of consulting, banking, investing, or business intelligence or market research experience\n\n - Strong analytical aptitude. You intuitively think about problems in terms of numbers and models, and you are able to quickly execute analyses in Excel or SQL. We will test you on this. You must feel comfortable with statistical tools and running methodologically sound surveys. Prior experience running brand surveys and creative testing is a plus.\n\n - Fluency with tools and using AI to work faster and smarter with data, and the judgement to know when the output is right and when it looks off.\n\n - Ability to present findings and recommendations to a senior leadership audience, fielding challenges and incorporating feedback.\n\n - Structured and logical thinker with the ability to quickly get up to speed on new industries, products, and challenges.\n\n - Self-driven and relentlessly proactive. You don’t need someone to tell you to “move”. You just move. We’d rather have to tell you to slow down than to speed up.\n   \n   \n\nComp: 150k - 185k\n\n\n\n\nOUR CULTURE & VALUES\n\n - We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.\n\n - We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.\n\n - We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.\n\n - We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nClick the link below to apply.\n\nWe reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.\n\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"4b53c96d-e950-494f-a03e-f377728df5e7","title":"Security Engineer, Corporate Security","department":"Security","team":"Security Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote USA","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-30T21:12:09.768+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/4b53c96d-e950-494f-a03e-f377728df5e7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/4b53c96d-e950-494f-a03e-f377728df5e7/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Cape</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected <em>and</em> have privacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>The Role</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are seeking an experienced Security Engineer with expertise in corporate security to join our team. As a strategic partner, you will make an immediate impact by leveraging your expertise across identity, endpoint, network, and information security alongside IT, engineering, and business teams. This role is pivotal in reducing risk across our corporate environment, covering employee-facing systems, internal infrastructure, and third-party risk, and will be responsible for designing, implementing, and maintaining security measures that comply with regulatory standards, enhance internal processes, and minimize data security risks. Through developing ongoing security strategies, technologies, and a strong security culture, you will support the organization's business objectives and daily operations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What You'll Work On</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, implement, and manage security controls and policies across corporate IT systems, focusing on the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of employee, customer, and business data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and mature identity and access management (IAM/SSO/MFA), endpoint security (EDR, MDM), and email/network security (phishing defense, DLP, firewalls, VPN) across the organization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform comprehensive security assessments of corporate systems and vendors to identify vulnerabilities, assess risk, and recommend actionable mitigation strategies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish governance, guardrails, and monitoring for emerging employee tooling, including the associated data-handling, access, and third-party risks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the vulnerability management lifecycle across the corporate fleet: scanning, risk-based prioritization, remediation and patch SLAs, and closure tracking across endpoints and internal systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead security awareness and phishing simulation programs to build an organization-wide culture of security.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to compliance and audit efforts as needed, lending security context where it helps the business move faster.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assess and manage third-party/vendor security risk, including security questionnaires, contract reviews, and ongoing vendor monitoring.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist in running and addressing findings from penetration tests, red team exercises, and internal audits, ensuring prompt and effective remediation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay informed about the latest security threats, vulnerabilities, and compliance mandates affecting corporate environments; provide strategic guidance on technologies and best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Investigate security incidents and insider-threat concerns in partnership with HR, Legal, and IT as needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raise the security bar across the company by mentoring engineers and partners on secure practices, fostering a culture of security awareness and continuous improvement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with stakeholders to integrate security requirements effectively into IT projects and broader business initiatives.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Experience</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Security, or a related field or equivalent experience. Advanced degrees or certifications (e.g., CISSP, GIAC, Security+, CISM) are advantageous.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A minimum of 2 years of experience in information security, with meaningful experience across corporate/IT security domains (identity, endpoint, network, GRC).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of enterprise identity providers and SSO/MFA platforms, endpoint/EDR tooling, MDM platforms, and email security tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of common compliance frameworks (e.g., SOC 2, ISO 27001).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with government/public-sector security frameworks (FedRAMP, FISMA, NIST SP 800 series, CJIS) is a plus, given Cape's government-facing customer base.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of consumer privacy regulations (GDPR, CCPA, and other regional privacy laws) as they apply to handling customer data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to secure software development lifecycle (SSDLC) practices and partnering with engineering on secure design reviews.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in scripting or automation (Python, shell scripting, or similar) to streamline security operations and reporting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with vendor/third-party risk management processes and tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid knowledge of network security, encryption technologies, and secure business-system configuration.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent analytical skills for identifying and mitigating complex security vulnerabilities and risks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and leadership abilities, capable of working collaboratively across teams and effectively conveying technical information to non-technical stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organized and able to manage multiple priorities in a dynamic, fast-paced environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Competencies</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Role competencies</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Security Expertise – Experience identifying and resolving security issues across corporate systems (identity, endpoint, network, and data). Secure-by-design principles, and partnering with IT/engineering during design time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analytical – Collects data and information; uses critical thinking to solve problems and make sound decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaboration &amp; Teamwork – Builds partnerships with others to reach common goals. Able to share credit with coworkers, display enthusiasm and promote a friendly group-working environment. Works closely with other departments as necessary, supports group decisions and solicits opinions from coworkers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communication – Presents information through verbal and written communication; reads and interprets complex information; listens well. Develops and delivers multi-mode communications that convey clear understanding of unique audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Decision-Making – Acts quickly to solve problems and exercises good judgment by making sound and well-informed decisions. Perceives the impact and implications of decisions; makes effective and timely decisions, even when data is limited.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Dependability/Self-Management – Possesses the personal discipline and diligence necessary to keep commitments and to complete tasks. Is accountable for actions and outcomes. Makes effort to improve situations without explicit instructions; a self-starter who consciously manages his/her own time and resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer Centric – Values the importance of delivering high quality, innovative service to employees; understands the needs of the client; responds promptly and is accessible to them; follows through on commitments in a timely manner; maintains positive, long-term working relationships; assumes ownership of process issues and takes appropriate steps to mitigate problems. Gets consistently high feedback from stakeholders. Raises hand to help.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexibility / Adaptability – Adjusts quickly to changing priorities, conditions, and challenges. Copes effectively with complexity and change. Is comfortable navigating ambiguity. Can handle business changes with ease and without frustration or a feeling of defeat. Feels comfortable dealing with limited unknowns in an area they are well versed in.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Planning &amp; Organization – Manages multiple projects, determines project urgency in a meaningful and practical way, uses goals to guide actions, creates detailed action plans, and organizes tasks.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape-specific competencies</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Do Excellent Work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respect The Opportunity (each other, the user)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Overshare</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bias Towards Action</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Compensation</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive compensation that is <strong>geo-adjusted</strong> based on <strong>your location,</strong> along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in<strong> New York, New York is $180,000-$220,000</strong> depending on experience and interview performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our benefits include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stipends for</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Family-forming needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gender-affirming care</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Culture &amp; Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How to apply</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Click the link below to apply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT CAPE\n\nCape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.\n\nInstead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected and have privacy.\n\nWe didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.\n\nToday, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM\n\nAt Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nWe are seeking an experienced Security Engineer with expertise in corporate security to join our team. As a strategic partner, you will make an immediate impact by leveraging your expertise across identity, endpoint, network, and information security alongside IT, engineering, and business teams. This role is pivotal in reducing risk across our corporate environment, covering employee-facing systems, internal infrastructure, and third-party risk, and will be responsible for designing, implementing, and maintaining security measures that comply with regulatory standards, enhance internal processes, and minimize data security risks. Through developing ongoing security strategies, technologies, and a strong security culture, you will support the organization's business objectives and daily operations.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL WORK ON\n\n - Design, implement, and manage security controls and policies across corporate IT systems, focusing on the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of employee, customer, and business data.\n\n - Own and mature identity and access management (IAM/SSO/MFA), endpoint security (EDR, MDM), and email/network security (phishing defense, DLP, firewalls, VPN) across the organization.\n\n - Perform comprehensive security assessments of corporate systems and vendors to identify vulnerabilities, assess risk, and recommend actionable mitigation strategies.\n\n - Establish governance, guardrails, and monitoring for emerging employee tooling, including the associated data-handling, access, and third-party risks.\n\n - Own the vulnerability management lifecycle across the corporate fleet: scanning, risk-based prioritization, remediation and patch SLAs, and closure tracking across endpoints and internal systems.\n\n - Lead security awareness and phishing simulation programs to build an organization-wide culture of security.\n\n - Contribute to compliance and audit efforts as needed, lending security context where it helps the business move faster.\n\n - Assess and manage third-party/vendor security risk, including security questionnaires, contract reviews, and ongoing vendor monitoring.\n\n - Assist in running and addressing findings from penetration tests, red team exercises, and internal audits, ensuring prompt and effective remediation.\n\n - Stay informed about the latest security threats, vulnerabilities, and compliance mandates affecting corporate environments; provide strategic guidance on technologies and best practices.\n\n - Investigate security incidents and insider-threat concerns in partnership with HR, Legal, and IT as needed.\n\n - Raise the security bar across the company by mentoring engineers and partners on secure practices, fostering a culture of security awareness and continuous improvement.\n\n - Collaborate with stakeholders to integrate security requirements effectively into IT projects and broader business initiatives.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n - Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Security, or a related field or equivalent experience. Advanced degrees or certifications (e.g., CISSP, GIAC, Security+, CISM) are advantageous.\n\n - A minimum of 2 years of experience in information security, with meaningful experience across corporate/IT security domains (identity, endpoint, network, GRC).\n\n - Deep understanding of enterprise identity providers and SSO/MFA platforms, endpoint/EDR tooling, MDM platforms, and email security tooling.\n\n - Working knowledge of common compliance frameworks (e.g., SOC 2, ISO 27001).\n\n - Familiarity with government/public-sector security frameworks (FedRAMP, FISMA, NIST SP 800 series, CJIS) is a plus, given Cape's government-facing customer base.\n\n - Working knowledge of consumer privacy regulations (GDPR, CCPA, and other regional privacy laws) as they apply to handling customer data.\n\n - Exposure to secure software development lifecycle (SSDLC) practices and partnering with engineering on secure design reviews.\n\n - Proficiency in scripting or automation (Python, shell scripting, or similar) to streamline security operations and reporting.\n\n - Familiarity with vendor/third-party risk management processes and tooling.\n\n - Solid knowledge of network security, encryption technologies, and secure business-system configuration.\n\n - Excellent analytical skills for identifying and mitigating complex security vulnerabilities and risks.\n\n - Strong communication and leadership abilities, capable of working collaboratively across teams and effectively conveying technical information to non-technical stakeholders.\n\n - Organized and able to manage multiple priorities in a dynamic, fast-paced environment.\n\n\n\nCompetencies\n\nRole competencies\n\n - Security Expertise – Experience identifying and resolving security issues across corporate systems (identity, endpoint, network, and data). Secure-by-design principles, and partnering with IT/engineering during design time.\n\n - Analytical – Collects data and information; uses critical thinking to solve problems and make sound decisions.\n\n - Collaboration & Teamwork – Builds partnerships with others to reach common goals. Able to share credit with coworkers, display enthusiasm and promote a friendly group-working environment. Works closely with other departments as necessary, supports group decisions and solicits opinions from coworkers.\n\n - Communication – Presents information through verbal and written communication; reads and interprets complex information; listens well. Develops and delivers multi-mode communications that convey clear understanding of unique audiences.\n\n - Decision-Making – Acts quickly to solve problems and exercises good judgment by making sound and well-informed decisions. Perceives the impact and implications of decisions; makes effective and timely decisions, even when data is limited.\n\n - Dependability/Self-Management – Possesses the personal discipline and diligence necessary to keep commitments and to complete tasks. Is accountable for actions and outcomes. Makes effort to improve situations without explicit instructions; a self-starter who consciously manages his/her own time and resources.\n\n - Customer Centric – Values the importance of delivering high quality, innovative service to employees; understands the needs of the client; responds promptly and is accessible to them; follows through on commitments in a timely manner; maintains positive, long-term working relationships; assumes ownership of process issues and takes appropriate steps to mitigate problems. Gets consistently high feedback from stakeholders. Raises hand to help.\n\n - Flexibility / Adaptability – Adjusts quickly to changing priorities, conditions, and challenges. Copes effectively with complexity and change. Is comfortable navigating ambiguity. Can handle business changes with ease and without frustration or a feeling of defeat. Feels comfortable dealing with limited unknowns in an area they are well versed in.\n\n - Planning & Organization – Manages multiple projects, determines project urgency in a meaningful and practical way, uses goals to guide actions, creates detailed action plans, and organizes tasks.\n\nCape-specific competencies\n\n - Do Excellent Work\n\n - Respect The Opportunity (each other, the user)\n\n - Overshare\n\n - Bias Towards Action\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nWe offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in New York, New York is $180,000-$220,000 depending on experience and interview performance.\n\nOur benefits include:\n\n - 401(k) match\n\n - 100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents\n\n - 12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)\n\n - Stipends for\n   \n   - Family-forming needs\n   \n   - Gender-affirming care\n\n - Unlimited PTO\n\n\n\n\nOUR CULTURE & VALUES\n\n - We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.\n\n - We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.\n\n - We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.\n\n - We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nClick the link below to apply.\n\nWe reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.\n\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"94f0de6b-710c-45cc-8113-7091b030f8e0","title":"Chief Information Security Officer (CISO)","department":"Security","team":"Security Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York, NY","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Washington DC","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Washington DC","addressCountry":"USA"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-07-30T17:42:02.779+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"450 Park Avenue South","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/94f0de6b-710c-45cc-8113-7091b030f8e0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/94f0de6b-710c-45cc-8113-7091b030f8e0/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Cape</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected <em>and</em> have privacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>The Role</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The CISO is our chief protector. Our infrastructure, threat model, and customer expectations are more complex than a typical mobile carrier or a typical software company. Your challenge is to enable rapid product innovation without compromising on our goal to be the most secure commercial mobile network on the planet. You'll own the strategy and execution of security across our network, products, and corporate systems and work as a partner to Engineering and the executive team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a build-and-defend role, not a maintain-the-status-quo role. You will immediately take ownership of a highly technical, responsive, and ambitious security, IT, and compliance org. Your mandate is to resource, mature, and scale this team to stay ahead of threats and enable Cape’s rapid growth.This role is based out of our NYC or DC office and reports to our founder and CEO John Doyle.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What You'll Work On</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own Cape's end-to-end security strategy — network infrastructure, product/application security, cloud and corporate IT, and physical/personnel security.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and lead a security team capable of defending a carrier-grade network against sophisticated, well-resourced adversaries, including nation-state actors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and drive the security architecture and controls for a cellular network we operate ourselves, from the radio access network through core infrastructure and subscriber data systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Engineering leadership to embed security into the product development lifecycle.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead teams conducting threat modeling, penetration testing, red-teaming, and incident response programs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set and communicate security policy to the board and executive team, translating technical risk into business terms and making tradeoffs with speed of execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vet and manage relationships with external security vendors, auditors, and researchers, including running a responsible disclosure / bug bounty program.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Champion a security-first culture across the entire company, not just within the security team.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Experience</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years in information security, with at least 5 years in a senior security leadership role (CISO, VP Security, Head of Security) at a company with meaningful infrastructure or regulatory complexity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Eligible and willing to obtain TS/SCI clearance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing geographically dispersed teams of engineers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of building security teams and programs from an early stage, not just operating a mature one you inherited.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep technical credibility — you can go toe-to-toe with your best engineers on architecture and risk, while also speaking fluently to executive leadership and the board.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A genuine belief that privacy and security are inseparable, and that protecting users sometimes means resisting internal and external pressure to compromise on either.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent judgment under ambiguity and the ability to move fast without cutting corners that matter.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">(Bonus Points) Direct experience securing telecom, network infrastructure, or other critical infrastructure — you understand things like SS7, radio networks, or core carrier systems, or you've secured environments of comparable complexity (e.g., cloud infrastructure providers, fintech, critical infrastructure).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">(Bonus Points) Experience securing an environment with Forward Deployed Engineers and the complexity around high risk travel.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Compensation</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in NYC/DC is <strong>$300,000 - $350,000 </strong>depending on experience and interview performance and location.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our benefits include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stipends for</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Family-forming needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gender-affirming care</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Relocation and moving assistance if needed</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Culture &amp; Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How to apply</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Click the link below to apply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT CAPE\n\nCape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.\n\nInstead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected and have privacy.\n\nWe didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.\n\nToday, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM\n\nAt Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nThe CISO is our chief protector. Our infrastructure, threat model, and customer expectations are more complex than a typical mobile carrier or a typical software company. Your challenge is to enable rapid product innovation without compromising on our goal to be the most secure commercial mobile network on the planet. You'll own the strategy and execution of security across our network, products, and corporate systems and work as a partner to Engineering and the executive team.\n\nThis is a build-and-defend role, not a maintain-the-status-quo role. You will immediately take ownership of a highly technical, responsive, and ambitious security, IT, and compliance org. Your mandate is to resource, mature, and scale this team to stay ahead of threats and enable Cape’s rapid growth.This role is based out of our NYC or DC office and reports to our founder and CEO John Doyle.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL WORK ON\n\n - Own Cape's end-to-end security strategy — network infrastructure, product/application security, cloud and corporate IT, and physical/personnel security.\n\n - Build and lead a security team capable of defending a carrier-grade network against sophisticated, well-resourced adversaries, including nation-state actors.\n\n - Design and drive the security architecture and controls for a cellular network we operate ourselves, from the radio access network through core infrastructure and subscriber data systems.\n\n - Partner closely with Engineering leadership to embed security into the product development lifecycle.\n\n - Lead teams conducting threat modeling, penetration testing, red-teaming, and incident response programs.\n\n - Set and communicate security policy to the board and executive team, translating technical risk into business terms and making tradeoffs with speed of execution.\n\n - Vet and manage relationships with external security vendors, auditors, and researchers, including running a responsible disclosure / bug bounty program.\n\n - Champion a security-first culture across the entire company, not just within the security team.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n - 10+ years in information security, with at least 5 years in a senior security leadership role (CISO, VP Security, Head of Security) at a company with meaningful infrastructure or regulatory complexity.\n\n - Eligible and willing to obtain TS/SCI clearance.\n\n - Experience managing geographically dispersed teams of engineers.\n\n - A track record of building security teams and programs from an early stage, not just operating a mature one you inherited.\n\n - Deep technical credibility — you can go toe-to-toe with your best engineers on architecture and risk, while also speaking fluently to executive leadership and the board.\n\n - A genuine belief that privacy and security are inseparable, and that protecting users sometimes means resisting internal and external pressure to compromise on either.\n\n - Excellent judgment under ambiguity and the ability to move fast without cutting corners that matter.\n\n - (Bonus Points) Direct experience securing telecom, network infrastructure, or other critical infrastructure — you understand things like SS7, radio networks, or core carrier systems, or you've secured environments of comparable complexity (e.g., cloud infrastructure providers, fintech, critical infrastructure).\n\n - (Bonus Points) Experience securing an environment with Forward Deployed Engineers and the complexity around high risk travel.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nWe offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in NYC/DC is $300,000 - $350,000 depending on experience and interview performance and location.\n\nOur benefits include:\n\n - 401(k) match\n\n - 100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents\n\n - 12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)\n\n - Stipends for\n   \n   - Family-forming needs\n   \n   - Gender-affirming care\n\n - Unlimited PTO\n\n - Relocation and moving assistance if needed\n\n\n\n\nOUR CULTURE & VALUES\n\n - We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.\n\n - We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.\n\n - We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.\n\n - We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nClick the link below to apply.\n\nWe reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.\n\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"f71e9ab6-2e7c-4a7b-9088-57a3e777ac6a","title":"Head of People","department":"Internal Ops","team":"Internal Ops","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York, NY","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-05T18:48:07.161+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"450 Park Avenue South","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/f71e9ab6-2e7c-4a7b-9088-57a3e777ac6a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/f71e9ab6-2e7c-4a7b-9088-57a3e777ac6a/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Cape</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected <em>and</em> have privacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mission</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape’s Head of People owns the talent strategy and human engine behind our growth. Our team is technical, creative, and relentless. Your job is to guide us through one of a company’s toughest inflection points: scaling from 100 to 300+ people without diluting talent or slowing execution.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will immediately take ownership of our People org—spanning Recruiting and HR—and build out the team, starting with hiring a Head of Recruiting. You will own the design and execution of the department’s roadmap, ensuring that the team builds best in class programs that makes Cape a top talent magnet.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The right leader naturally stays close to the floor—sourcing key talent, staying plugged into employee sentiment, and keeping feedback loops tight across every level of the company.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reporting directly to founder and CEO John Doyle, you will sit on the leadership team and bring a key POV to company-level decisions.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Objectives</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Hire:</strong> Build a recruiting engine that attracts top talent. This includes optimizing capacity and tooling, elevating business partnerships, improving process efficiency, and nailing planning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Retain:</strong> Elevate the employee experience to achieve above industry retention, viral referrals, and continuous engagement. This includes making clear investments in total rewards, people systems, and career progression.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow People:</strong> Plan and execute our transition from a team of 100 Swiss Army Knives defined by Herculean individual efforts to a company of 300+. This includes refining organization structure, formalizing career advancement, and retooling performance reviews and succession planning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Scale the Team:</strong> Professionalize our approach to management to maintain Cape’s culture, execute at scale, and develop extraordinary talent. This includes automating where possible, establishing clear career paths and associated expectations, hiring top-notch leaders, and formalizing a management training program.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">NY (preferred)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">DC (with frequent NY travel)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you bring</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of progressive People experience, including 3-5 years in a leadership role, and direct participation in Recruiting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Significant experience in a high-growth startup where you built People processes and teams from the early stages.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong command of core People functions: talent acquisition, compensation, performance management, and daily operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-functional depth: experience in working with executive and business unit leaders across the organization.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$275,000-350,000</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Culture &amp; Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How to apply</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Click the link below to apply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT CAPE\n\nCape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.\n\nInstead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected and have privacy.\n\nWe didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.\n\nToday, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM\n\nAt Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.\n\n\n\nMission\n\nCape’s Head of People owns the talent strategy and human engine behind our growth. Our team is technical, creative, and relentless. Your job is to guide us through one of a company’s toughest inflection points: scaling from 100 to 300+ people without diluting talent or slowing execution.\n\nYou will immediately take ownership of our People org—spanning Recruiting and HR—and build out the team, starting with hiring a Head of Recruiting. You will own the design and execution of the department’s roadmap, ensuring that the team builds best in class programs that makes Cape a top talent magnet.\n\nThe right leader naturally stays close to the floor—sourcing key talent, staying plugged into employee sentiment, and keeping feedback loops tight across every level of the company.\n\nReporting directly to founder and CEO John Doyle, you will sit on the leadership team and bring a key POV to company-level decisions.\n\n \n\nKey Objectives\n\n - Hire: Build a recruiting engine that attracts top talent. This includes optimizing capacity and tooling, elevating business partnerships, improving process efficiency, and nailing planning.\n\n - Retain: Elevate the employee experience to achieve above industry retention, viral referrals, and continuous engagement. This includes making clear investments in total rewards, people systems, and career progression.\n\n - Grow People: Plan and execute our transition from a team of 100 Swiss Army Knives defined by Herculean individual efforts to a company of 300+. This includes refining organization structure, formalizing career advancement, and retooling performance reviews and succession planning.\n\n - Scale the Team: Professionalize our approach to management to maintain Cape’s culture, execute at scale, and develop extraordinary talent. This includes automating where possible, establishing clear career paths and associated expectations, hiring top-notch leaders, and formalizing a management training program.\n\nLocation\n\n - NY (preferred)\n\n - DC (with frequent NY travel)\n\nWhat you bring\n\n - 10+ years of progressive People experience, including 3-5 years in a leadership role, and direct participation in Recruiting.\n\n - Significant experience in a high-growth startup where you built People processes and teams from the early stages.\n\n - Strong command of core People functions: talent acquisition, compensation, performance management, and daily operations.\n\n - Cross-functional depth: experience in working with executive and business unit leaders across the organization.\n\nSalary Range\n\n - $275,000-350,000\n\n\n\n\nOUR CULTURE & VALUES\n\n - We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.\n\n - We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.\n\n - We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.\n\n - We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nClick the link below to apply.\n\nWe reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.\n\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"c8a93382-467f-46c5-9881-9f47ad531ef9","title":"HR Operations","department":"Internal Ops","team":"People","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York, NY","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-25T16:53:03.241+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"450 Park Avenue South","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/c8a93382-467f-46c5-9881-9f47ad531ef9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/c8a93382-467f-46c5-9881-9f47ad531ef9/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Cape</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected <em>and</em> have privacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>The Role</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is growing its People Team! We are looking for a HR Operations Associate to work cross-functionally with partners in Finance, Recruiting, HR and IT to help keep our back of house processes running as fast as Cape is growing. <br /><br />The right candidate treats every process and every request as an opportunity to keep the company moving smoothly. They develop practical and creative ways to support Capers day-to-day, creating a world-class employee experience from onboarding through every touchpoint after. They use data and meticulous organization to track progress, flag bottlenecks, and set a new bar for process and quality. This is a fast-paced, passionate environment in explosive growth mode. We need you to bring precision and care to every detail as Cape continues to scale. </p><h1><strong><br /><br />What You'll Work On</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Reporting &amp; triage:</strong> Run recurring new-hire/headcount reports for Finance and Leadership, and serve as first responder for employee HR questions, resolving what you can and routing the rest to the right owner.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Onboarding:</strong> Be the bridge between Recruiting, HR and Leadership - track visa processes,  coordinate IT/facility access, and run orientations that get people set up and ready to do their best work from day one.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Employee Support:</strong> Serve as the trusted first point of contact for the team. Answering day-to-day questions on leave, benefits, and company policy with clarity and care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Payroll &amp; Benefits Assistance:</strong> Keep the details right. Track leave, employee status and hand off clean, accurate data to payroll on schedule to Sequoia, along with any relevant payroll adjustments throughout the employee lifecycle. Work closely with Cape’s PEO (Sequoia), EoR (Remote), and leave platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Reporting &amp; Compliance:</strong> Draft verification letters, compile core HR metrics, and help keep us compliant. Maintain and update physical and digital employee files in our HRIS with rigor and discretion. Pull accurate reporting for finance and build dashboards that will give leadership insights to help Cape scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Scale Cape:</strong> Work to make sure our back of house process matches the size and stage of the organization as we scale and onboard more people. Suggest and help build processes, author employee FAQs and assist in the success of other People programs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Experience</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years in HR Operations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An instinct for automating repetitive HR workflows (forms, reminders, reporting) rather than doing them by hand each time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Led and coordinated payroll processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HRIS experience; Sequoia experience required</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in NYC is $100-130k depending on experience and interview performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our benefits include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stipends for</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Family-forming needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gender-affirming care</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Culture &amp; Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How to apply</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Click the link below to apply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT CAPE\n\nCape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.\n\nInstead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected and have privacy.\n\nWe didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.\n\nToday, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM\n\nAt Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nCape is growing its People Team! We are looking for a HR Operations Associate to work cross-functionally with partners in Finance, Recruiting, HR and IT to help keep our back of house processes running as fast as Cape is growing. \n\nThe right candidate treats every process and every request as an opportunity to keep the company moving smoothly. They develop practical and creative ways to support Capers day-to-day, creating a world-class employee experience from onboarding through every touchpoint after. They use data and meticulous organization to track progress, flag bottlenecks, and set a new bar for process and quality. This is a fast-paced, passionate environment in explosive growth mode. We need you to bring precision and care to every detail as Cape continues to scale. \n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL WORK ON\n\nReporting & triage: Run recurring new-hire/headcount reports for Finance and Leadership, and serve as first responder for employee HR questions, resolving what you can and routing the rest to the right owner.\n\nOnboarding: Be the bridge between Recruiting, HR and Leadership - track visa processes,  coordinate IT/facility access, and run orientations that get people set up and ready to do their best work from day one.\n\nEmployee Support: Serve as the trusted first point of contact for the team. Answering day-to-day questions on leave, benefits, and company policy with clarity and care.\n\nPayroll & Benefits Assistance: Keep the details right. Track leave, employee status and hand off clean, accurate data to payroll on schedule to Sequoia, along with any relevant payroll adjustments throughout the employee lifecycle. Work closely with Cape’s PEO (Sequoia), EoR (Remote), and leave platform.\n\nReporting & Compliance: Draft verification letters, compile core HR metrics, and help keep us compliant. Maintain and update physical and digital employee files in our HRIS with rigor and discretion. Pull accurate reporting for finance and build dashboards that will give leadership insights to help Cape scale.\n\nScale Cape: Work to make sure our back of house process matches the size and stage of the organization as we scale and onboard more people. Suggest and help build processes, author employee FAQs and assist in the success of other People programs.\n\n\n\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n - 4+ years in HR Operations\n\n - An instinct for automating repetitive HR workflows (forms, reminders, reporting) rather than doing them by hand each time\n\n - Led and coordinated payroll processes\n\n - HRIS experience; Sequoia experience required\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nWe offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in NYC is $100-130k depending on experience and interview performance.\n\nOur benefits include:\n\n - 401(k) match\n\n - 100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents\n\n - 12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)\n\n - Stipends for\n   \n   - Family-forming needs\n   \n   - Gender-affirming care\n\n - Unlimited PTO\n\n\n\n\nOUR CULTURE & VALUES\n\n - We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.\n\n - We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.\n\n - We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.\n\n - We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nClick the link below to apply.\n\nWe reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.\n\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"b15f165f-8bc2-474f-8c83-748f43397221","title":"Technical Program Manager, Security","department":"Security","team":"Security Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote USA","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-31T13:31:41.845+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/b15f165f-8bc2-474f-8c83-748f43397221","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/b15f165f-8bc2-474f-8c83-748f43397221/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Cape</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected <em>and</em> have privacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>The Role</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is hiring our first Security Technical Program Manager, a rare chance to build this function from scratch inside a company where security is the product. You'll directly integrate with Security Engineering across  their three pillars: detection and response , corporate security , and product security. Rather than specializing in one lane, you'll use your visibility of the whole board to set priorities, define success, and increase velocity.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll also be the connective tissue between security engineering and Cape's broader ~70-person engineering organization, managing speed-security tradeoffs that are becoming more complex as AI tools proliferate. The metrics you create will steer company-wide policy and prioritization, and your judgment will drive the company SBOM.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What You'll Work On</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and communicate the security program's strategy, priorities, and progress to the broader business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Shape how Cape brings new security tools into the fold, from vendor procurement through implementation, powering the stack that keeps our security org running.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Keep the security engineering team on track — manage priorities, maintain the backlog, and drive execution across detection &amp; response, corporate security, and product security.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the technical go-between for security engineers and Cape's ~70 product engineers, translating security requirements and risk into terms product teams can act on, and vice versa.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with security engineering leadership to plan roadmaps, run program rituals, and unblock cross-team dependencies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build trust and clear communication channels with engineering stakeholders across the company.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Experience</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience as a TPM or PM embedded with a security team that builds tooling and systems in-house.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid grounding in computer engineering fundamentals; comfortable going deep on technical detail with engineers across detection &amp; response, corporate security, and product security.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of defining and communicating technical programs to non-technical stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong prioritization and backlog management skills, with the judgment to know what matters most.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating as a trusted technical liaison between specialized teams and a large, distributed engineering organization.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Compensation</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role $180,000 - $230,000 depending on level, experience, and interview performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our benefits include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stipends for</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Family-forming needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gender-affirming care</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Culture &amp; Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How to apply</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Click the link below to apply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT CAPE\n\nCape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.\n\nInstead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected and have privacy.\n\nWe didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.\n\nToday, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM\n\nAt Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nCape is hiring our first Security Technical Program Manager, a rare chance to build this function from scratch inside a company where security is the product. You'll directly integrate with Security Engineering across  their three pillars: detection and response , corporate security , and product security. Rather than specializing in one lane, you'll use your visibility of the whole board to set priorities, define success, and increase velocity.\n\nYou'll also be the connective tissue between security engineering and Cape's broader ~70-person engineering organization, managing speed-security tradeoffs that are becoming more complex as AI tools proliferate. The metrics you create will steer company-wide policy and prioritization, and your judgment will drive the company SBOM.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL WORK ON\n\n - Define and communicate the security program's strategy, priorities, and progress to the broader business.\n\n - Shape how Cape brings new security tools into the fold, from vendor procurement through implementation, powering the stack that keeps our security org running.\n\n - Keep the security engineering team on track — manage priorities, maintain the backlog, and drive execution across detection & response, corporate security, and product security.\n\n - Serve as the technical go-between for security engineers and Cape's ~70 product engineers, translating security requirements and risk into terms product teams can act on, and vice versa.\n\n - Partner with security engineering leadership to plan roadmaps, run program rituals, and unblock cross-team dependencies.\n\n - Build trust and clear communication channels with engineering stakeholders across the company.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n - Prior experience as a TPM or PM embedded with a security team that builds tooling and systems in-house.\n\n - Solid grounding in computer engineering fundamentals; comfortable going deep on technical detail with engineers across detection & response, corporate security, and product security.\n\n - Track record of defining and communicating technical programs to non-technical stakeholders.\n\n - Strong prioritization and backlog management skills, with the judgment to know what matters most.\n\n - Comfort operating as a trusted technical liaison between specialized teams and a large, distributed engineering organization.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nWe offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role $180,000 - $230,000 depending on level, experience, and interview performance.\n\nOur benefits include:\n\n - 401(k) match\n\n - 100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents\n\n - 12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)\n\n - Stipends for\n\n - Family-forming needs\n\n - Gender-affirming care\n\n - Unlimited PTO\n\n\n\n\nOUR CULTURE & VALUES\n\n - We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.\n\n - We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.\n\n - We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.\n\n - We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nClick the link below to apply.\n\nWe reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.\n\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"8b844b20-8345-4291-8bfb-25c7bf34ec62","title":"Account Executive, Navy ","department":"Business Development","team":"AE","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Arlington, VA","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-31T14:52:47.133+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Virginia","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Arlington"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/8b844b20-8345-4291-8bfb-25c7bf34ec62","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/cape/8b844b20-8345-4291-8bfb-25c7bf34ec62/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Cape</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected <em>and</em> have privacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>The Role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Account Executive at Cape, your mission is to drive revenue growth by effectively positioning our proprietary privacy and security first solutions to the United States Navy. You will act as a trusted advisor, understanding the unique needs of government clients, navigating the complexities of government procurement, and delivering solutions that align with their missions. Your role is pivotal in establishing Cape as a key partner to the Navy, ensuring both immediate sales success and long-term strategic relationships.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What You'll Work On</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Revenue Generation: </strong>Achieve or exceed annual sales targets by closing new business deals with the Navy. Expand the Cape’s footprint within existing government accounts by identifying and pursuing upsell and cross-sell opportunities.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strategic Account Management: </strong>Develop and execute comprehensive account plans for key Navy engagements, including strategies for relationship building, opportunity identification, and long-term account growth. Maintain deep knowledge of government procurement processes and contracting vehicles, ensuring successful navigation through complex sales cycles (such as the DOW’s Planning, Programming, Budgeting, and Execution (PPBE) and Program Objective Memorandum (POM) processes).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Pipeline Development: </strong>Build and maintain a robust sales pipeline through proactive outreach, relationship building, and effective lead generation strategies. Collaborate with marketing and business development teams to identify new opportunities and generate qualified leads.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Client Satisfaction and Retention: </strong>Deliver exceptional client service by understanding and addressing the needs of USG clients, leading to high levels of satisfaction and long-term partnerships. Serve as the primary point of contact for government clients, ensuring smooth communication, timely responses, and effective resolution of any issues or concerns.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Market and Competitive Intelligence: </strong>Stay informed about industry trends, government initiatives, and competitive landscape to position Cape as a leading solution provider in the government sector. Provide feedback to product and marketing teams on market needs and competitive intelligence, contributing to the continuous improvement of Cape’s offerings.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Experience</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience working in customer-facing roles (account executive, customer success, solutions engineer, or related discipline), or equivalent government experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or related field, or equivalent hands-on experience, including the ability to quickly develop and tailor scripts or technical solutions to meet customer deployment needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gritty technical skills. We don’t need you to be shipping code to prod. But you enjoy automating tasks as necessary to make sure we deliver for our customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Domain experience in cyber operations, privacy, security, telecommunications or related fields.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in enterprise sales, especially at early stage companies focused on defense.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional written and verbal communication skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adaptive and introspective; willing to learn, guide, lead and follow.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Active U.S. TS/SCI clearance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willingness to travel up to 75%.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Based in DC or New York. Relocation assistance available.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Compensation:</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive compensation that is <strong>geo-adjusted</strong> based on <strong>your location</strong>, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in Washington, DC is $180-200K depending on experience and interview performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our benefits include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stipends for</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Family-forming needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gender-affirming care</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Culture &amp; Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How to apply</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Click the link below to apply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT CAPE\n\nCape is America’s privacy-first mobile carrier. Our mission is to be a force for good in global wireless. Cape was founded in 2022 by people who believe privacy is a fundamental right, not a luxury to be traded away. Our journey began when our founder recognized a critical vulnerability in our modern world: everyone relies on the same stagnant cellular infrastructure and legacy systems that track our every movement, monitor and profile our connections, and lose and sell our personal data.\n\nInstead of accepting the status quo, we decided to fix it. National security professionals, journalists, parents, and everyone in between can stay connected and have privacy.\n\nWe didn’t just build a layer on top of old tech; we built America’s most private and secure mobile carrier from the ground up. By building our own network from scratch, we are able to design and build a suite of privacy and security features that no other carrier on the planet can offer.\n\nToday, Cape provides our secure network to consumers, businesses, and government agencies alike. We closed our Series C in March 2026, and we are scaling rapidly, with the goal of giving people back control of their most personal information.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TEAM\n\nAt Cape, we are the architects of a privacy-centric movement that is just getting started. We are relentless builders, constantly innovating at the edge of what's possible in telecommunications. We operate on a foundation of high trust and high expectations. Our structure is flat, and collaboration matters more than hierarchy. As a member of our team, you will collaborate with world-class engineers, architects, and visionaries, and work across organizational lines to solve \"impossible\" problems and deliver mission-critical results for our users every single day.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nAs an Account Executive at Cape, your mission is to drive revenue growth by effectively positioning our proprietary privacy and security first solutions to the United States Navy. You will act as a trusted advisor, understanding the unique needs of government clients, navigating the complexities of government procurement, and delivering solutions that align with their missions. Your role is pivotal in establishing Cape as a key partner to the Navy, ensuring both immediate sales success and long-term strategic relationships.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL WORK ON\n\nRevenue Generation: Achieve or exceed annual sales targets by closing new business deals with the Navy. Expand the Cape’s footprint within existing government accounts by identifying and pursuing upsell and cross-sell opportunities.\n\nStrategic Account Management: Develop and execute comprehensive account plans for key Navy engagements, including strategies for relationship building, opportunity identification, and long-term account growth. Maintain deep knowledge of government procurement processes and contracting vehicles, ensuring successful navigation through complex sales cycles (such as the DOW’s Planning, Programming, Budgeting, and Execution (PPBE) and Program Objective Memorandum (POM) processes).\n\nPipeline Development: Build and maintain a robust sales pipeline through proactive outreach, relationship building, and effective lead generation strategies. Collaborate with marketing and business development teams to identify new opportunities and generate qualified leads.\n\nClient Satisfaction and Retention: Deliver exceptional client service by understanding and addressing the needs of USG clients, leading to high levels of satisfaction and long-term partnerships. Serve as the primary point of contact for government clients, ensuring smooth communication, timely responses, and effective resolution of any issues or concerns.\n\nMarket and Competitive Intelligence: Stay informed about industry trends, government initiatives, and competitive landscape to position Cape as a leading solution provider in the government sector. Provide feedback to product and marketing teams on market needs and competitive intelligence, contributing to the continuous improvement of Cape’s offerings.\n\n\n\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n - 5+ years of experience working in customer-facing roles (account executive, customer success, solutions engineer, or related discipline), or equivalent government experience.\n\n - Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or related field, or equivalent hands-on experience, including the ability to quickly develop and tailor scripts or technical solutions to meet customer deployment needs.\n\n - Gritty technical skills. We don’t need you to be shipping code to prod. But you enjoy automating tasks as necessary to make sure we deliver for our customers.\n\n - Domain experience in cyber operations, privacy, security, telecommunications or related fields.\n\n - Experience in enterprise sales, especially at early stage companies focused on defense.\n\n - Exceptional written and verbal communication skills.\n\n - Adaptive and introspective; willing to learn, guide, lead and follow.\n\n - Active U.S. TS/SCI clearance.\n\n - Willingness to travel up to 75%.\n\n - Based in DC or New York. Relocation assistance available.\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION:\n\nWe offer competitive compensation that is geo-adjusted based on your location, along with meaningful equity so you share in the value you help create. Salary range for this role in Washington, DC is $180-200K depending on experience and interview performance.\n\nOur benefits include:\n\n - 401(k) match\n\n - Unlimited PTO\n\n - 100% coverage of medical, dental, and vision premiums for you and your dependents\n\n - 12 weeks paid parental leave (for all parents, no waiting period)\n\n - Stipends for\n   \n   - Family-forming needs\n   \n   - Gender-affirming care\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOUR CULTURE & VALUES\n\n - We hire excellent people, give them outsized responsibility, and trust them to execute. Every person at Cape has a proven track record of tackling hard problems and winning.\n\n - We believe that personal privacy and national security are not at odds, and that they can be reconciled through strong technology.\n\n - We believe companies exist to build awesome things and take care of the people who build them, so we offer top-tier healthcare, 401(k) matching, and a generous vacation policy that our team actually uses to recharge.\n\n - We believe that a stronger company and a better product are built by people from all walks of life. We hire without regard to race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, disability, or Veteran status. If you are great at what you do, you belong here.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW TO APPLY\n\nClick the link below to apply.\n\nWe reserve the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes received from outside recruiting agencies and / or individual recruiters without being responsible for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes.\n\nWe are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, and without regard to disability or status as a protected veteran, or any other status protected by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}